{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions","id":1490573,"title":"[All eras]Some lore questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-17T18:42:07-07:00","id":1490573,"title":"[All eras]Some lore questions","content":"1. Is there any tie between the Terat Sin-Eater and S.K. Bhurano? Both were in India, albeit in different time-periods, and both dealt with Corruption, albeit with different focus for each woman.<br /> <br /> 2. Have named novas from TC Aberrant been mentioned or involved in TC Aeon? I\u2019m quite knowledgeable about 1e Aberrant, but 2e is, in some ways, a reimagining of the setting, so things may\u2019ve changed between editions.<br /> <br /> 3. Are psionics heritable? Is the child of a psion a psiad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-17-2022, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T19:12:36-07:00","id":1490574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions#post1490573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is there any tie between the Terat Sin-Eater and S.K. Bhurano? Both were in India, albeit in different time-periods, and both dealt with Corruption, albeit with different focus for each woman.<br /> <br /> 2. Have named novas from TC Aberrant been mentioned or involved in TC Aeon? I\u2019m quite knowledgeable about 1e Aberrant, but 2e is, in some ways, a reimagining of the setting, so things may\u2019ve changed between editions.<br /> <br /> 3. Are psionics heritable? Is the child of a psion a psiad?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Nothing is mentioned (and Sin-Eater hasn't been mentioned yet in Aberrant 2E to best the of my knowledge). Aeon notes... &quot;[Dr. Bhurano] began her studies in private, attending and later working at more than a dozen universities and research labs from the middle of the 20th century until the end of the 21st, taking on several different identities, and amassing more knowledge about noetic and quantum powers than anyone who had ever lived.&quot; It's possible they crossed paths, but Dr. Burano wasn't active solely in India or anything. It sounds like she didn't develop a deep interest in Corruption until she saw major Corruption Zones later in the wars, but with her focus on understanding what was happening she probably studied Quantum Flux Syndrome before then.<br /> <br /> 2. Aeon does mention a number of named Aberrants, and discusses the history of a few, but I don't think any of those are described in Aberrant. If I remember correctly there is a stretch goal from the Aberrant kickstarter to release a book of novas (Novas Worldwide I think?) that is getting close to finished. I wouldn't be surprised if some of the named Aberrants from Aeon show up there as easter eggs. Generally speaking TC has tried to avoid too much &quot;this is the future of a specific character&quot; type stuff in favor of letting things like that play out at individual tables.<br /> <br /> 3. Nothing has been written about it so far, but presumably there is a genetic component. It seems more likely that the child of a psion or psiad has a higher than usual chance of being a latent. A lot of the under the hood type stuff of how things really work hasn't really been delved into yet, so it might work way different. Notably when Dr. Bhurano used an invention to release a huge pulse of noetic energy and heal the Corruption Zones the energy also created tons of new Talents and latents, but not psiads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T19:29:00-07:00","id":1490576,"title":"","content":"So latency is more common a heritage? Ok! Thanks!<br /> <br /> 1. Are the Doyen mentioned at all in TC Aberrant or TC Anima?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T19:31:48-07:00","id":1490577,"title":"","content":"The named Aberrants from Aeon are mostly in the Aeon Expansion, the ones that specifically mention being from Earth are...<br /> <br /> <b>Slaughtermane</b> - Used to have a fan club, doesn't say what he was famous for or if Slaughtermane is the name he went by before the wars<br /> <b>Sandoval</b> <b>Gutierrez</b> - Kept a low profile before and during the wars and remained on Earth in hiding<br /> <b>Gouge</b> - We know she left Earth due to the Ultimatum, and is afraid to go back, but nothing about her life on Earth<br /> <br /> I think Zeus is the name of the Aberrant who hurled the Esperanza at Paris, and think he's noted to have fought in the Aberrant Wars. Forget which book he is mentioned in.<br /> <br /> The Crimson Saint is one of the Aberrants who rode the Esperanza down to Earth, they travel the ruins of France healing the sick and recruiting followers the most devout of which are mutated. No mention of a life on Earth.<br /> <br /> Distant Worlds (a supplement for Aeon discussing planets outside the Solar System) also mentions a number of Aberrants by name, mostly in relation to lost colonies founded by novas before the wars. I don't any of them are mentioned in Aberrant though.<br /> <br /> Terra Firma (a supplement for Aeon about Earth and the Solar System) also name drops a few Aberrants, usually in relation to the lingering effects of what they did during the wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T19:35:22-07:00","id":1490578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490576#post1490576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So latency is more common a heritage? Ok! Thanks!<br /> <br /> 1. Are the Doyen mentioned at all in TC Aberrant or TC Anima?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Anima reader - Doyen are mentioned only in Secrets chapter of era - and only in context ' they build force field that limit Novas till Devis Mal shannenigans'. - i. E. Main Aeon Timeline stuff. <br /> <br /> However, Anima is very much based on other aliens - Ascendancy... \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T19:59:14-07:00","id":1490581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490576#post1490576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So latency is more common a heritage? Ok! Thanks!<br /> <br /> 1. Are the Doyen mentioned at all in TC Aberrant or TC Anima?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Doyen get mentioned a lot across lots of TC books, but they're most active and involved in the affairs of humanity during the Aeon era.<br /> <br /> In Aberrant it notes that after the Adventure era the Doyen built an energy barrier around Earth to mute the effects of any future Hammersmith type events. N-Day was caused by Divis Mal recreating a quantum focused version of the Hammersmith event powerful enough to shatter the barrier, freaking out the Doyen. For some of the events in Aberrant that don't have specific defined causes the Doyen are mentioned as possible instigators, but one of several options.<br /> <br /> In Anima they're only mentioned once briefly, and then just in reference to the backstory of the big bads of Anima not as active meddlers in human affairs of that era. Presumably they were busy dealing with the effects of the Aberrants driven off Earth, and were hoping humanity would just die out after the wars. They don't take an active interest in earth again until Dr. Bhurano sets off a huge pulse of noetic energy, which leads to a faction of Doyen deciding to create the proxies and use humanity as catspaws against the Aberrants.<br /> <br /> In Adventure they're mentioned a few times, but mostly delving into more details about the energy barrier they built around Earth. An unintended, but positive from the Doyen point of view, effect of the barrier is it prevented any Inspired individual ever becoming powerful enough to go from Stalwart or Mesmerist to Nova or Psiad. The future Divis Mal and Dr. Bhurano both (separately) spent a lot of time trying to understand the Hammersmith Event, and were sort of aware something was interfering in a way that didn't make sense, but nothing indicates either of them ever became fully aware of the barrier or who created it.<br /> <br /> In Aether, the victorian era setting that is wrapping up its kickstarter this week, the Doyen are also mentioned, but again mostly in relation to the big bad of the setting (who are quantum users) and trying to bring about their downfall. The Doyen are seemingly unaware of Earth and humanity at this point in time, and don't get involved in the invasion of Earth.<br /> <br /> If you want more tasty Doyen info Under Alien Skies (an Aeon supplement delving into alien species) has a whole section on the Doyen and details their homeworld. The Qin also have a colony on a planet detailed in Distant Worlds that was once home to a Doyen colony before their failed attempt at ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T20:34:11-07:00","id":1490586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions#post1490573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Are psionics heritable? Is the child of a psion a psiad?</div> </div> </div> </div>All three of the power sources (quantum, psi, dimensional flux) are accessed by many of the same gene sequences. If you have the correct genes and are exposed to quantum energy, you may erupt as a nova. Exposure to noetic energy may turn you into a psiad. Exposure to raw flux may turn you into a Talent. Adventure! specifically notes it is rare but possible for someone to gain powers when someone who already has powers uses those powers on them, and that they always gain the same type of power as that person.<br /> <br /> Max Mercer is a Talent, but his supposed granddaughter is a psiad. I say supposed, because Maggie Mercer's father popped up one day in the '50s as a fully grown adult, announced himself as Max's son, and took over the Aeon Society. Max (who is asexual) didn't object, and won't say anything about his &quot;son's&quot; unnamed mother.<br /> <br /> As for whether psions can have psiad kids, it hasn't been explicitly addressed. On the one hand, it makes sense that it could happen. On the other hand, the Doyen are a bunch of dicks, and it wouldn't surprise me if they designed the prometheus chambers to interfere with the propagation of psi powers to future generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T01:41:17-07:00","id":1490588,"title":"","content":"One name that is mentioned both in Aeon (Terra Firma) and Aberrant is Vladimir Sierka, while he is not on Earth during Aeon Era, one of his supertech creations is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T01:42:14-07:00","id":1490589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions#post1490573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Are psionics heritable? Is the child of a psion a psiad?</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn\u2019t been addressed officially, and possibly never will be, but my own view is almost certainly not. Two psion parents probably a higher chance of producing latency, but essentially *zero* chance of making a psiad. One psion and a psiad - high chance of latency, maybe a chance of being a psiad. One psion and a baseline - slightly higher chance of latency, very little chance of producing a psiad..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T18:52:50-07:00","id":1490670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions#post1490573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is there any tie between the Terat Sin-Eater and S.K. Bhurano? Both were in India, albeit in different time-periods, and both dealt with Corruption, albeit with different focus for each woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2022 there are 1.38 billion people in India. That's a solid one out of every seven people in the world.<br /> <br /> Assuming half are women, that's still 690 million. Odds are two of them are going to have the same general interests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Have named novas from TC Aberrant been mentioned or involved in TC Aeon? </div> </div> </div>A few. Several that have been mentioned aren't using the same names they used in the Aberrant era.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T01:52:51-07:00","id":1490685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490670#post1490670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few. Several that have been mentioned aren't using the same names they used in the Aberrant era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will we see an official list? I understand one can say, yes, this and this can be the same, but will we see the future villainous names of our friendly novas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T08:02:54-07:00","id":1490711,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Ian! I\u2019m grateful you chimed in! Thank you, sir!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T09:50:25-07:00","id":1490886,"title":"","content":"Well, I got Trinity Continuum Aberrant Corebook, as well as a mini-sourcebook detailing a team of starting-level novas (\u201cAmalgamated Idea Dynamics\u201d). I\u2019m very glad I made both purchases, as I feel they were worth every single cent.<br /> <br /> Some things I\u2019ve already noticed:<br /> <br /> 1. The updated timeline. Makes the game more relevant.<br /> 2. Doing away with the death of a certain redhead. <br /> 3. The general tone of optimism. Granted, I, personally, stick to the canon timeline, so in my games this optimism will burn like wood in a chimney, but I loved it nonetheless, this ambience of limitless potential.<br /> 4. Fixing a certain metamorphic process unique to a certain radical nova faction. <i>Thank you!</i><br /> 5. A much better powers systems. I\u2019ve noticed some Mutants and Masterminds influences, but that is <i>not</i> an insult, but rather intended as a compliment.<br /> 6. They have a more coherent, less intrigue-y setting. This is good, because mundane conspiracies don\u2019t last long against characters with Mega-Manipulation and Mega-Intellect.<br /> 7. The art is <i>amazing</i>!<br /> <br /> I have no real complaints of any substance.<br /> <br /> As to Amalgamated Idea Dynamics, this lil sourcebook is <i>extremely</i> well done. Each character on the team is distinctive, and you can, in your mind, roughly see where each character could go, as the timeline moves along and powers rise.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I just wanted to say, \u201cSlaughtermane\u201d is one of <i>the</i> most <i>badass</i> names I\u2019ve ever heard of. Paints a picture in your mind just by the name alone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-21-2022, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T12:26:20-07:00","id":1490911,"title":"","content":"Some questions, concerning TC Aberrant:<br /> <br /> 1. Can Mega-Attributes go above 5 dots? I know the relevant Attribute would have to match the Mega-Attribute, but is this possible?<br /> 2. The Animal Mastery Mefa-Edge: does it work on alien wildlife?<br /> 3. Can the Detection Mega-Edge sense subquantum, the way psions can detect Quantum (\u201cCorruption\u201d)?<br /> 4. Would the Universal Translator Mega-Edge work on languages of an extremely alien nature (ie, the color-based language of Chromatics)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T12:59:45-07:00","id":1490915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490911#post1490911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some questions, concerning TC Aberrant:<br /> <br /> 1. Can Mega-Attributes go above 5 dots? I know the relevant Attribute would have to match the Mega-Attribute, but is this possible?<br /> 2. The Animal Mastery Mefa-Edge: does it work on alien wildlife?<br /> 3. Can the Detection Mega-Edge sense subquantum, the way psions can detect Quantum (\u201cCorruption\u201d)?<br /> 4. Would the Universal Translator Mega-Edge work on languages of an extremely alien nature (ie, the color-based language of Chromatics)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Yes, you need Quantum equal to the desired dots and the attribute at 5 dots<br /> 2. Up to you. Personally I would say no, and make it cost one extra dot to do so.<br /> 3. Why not? My personal answer is no, because Psi is too small to be detected, but the rules for Novas can also be used to describe Psiads, and so a Psiad could do (and basically alwals can do because its basically Attunement).<br /> 4. Up to you. Personally I would make it harder to do so, specially if the character cant reply (cant change color as in the example), but definetly not impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T14:32:23-07:00","id":1490932,"title":"","content":"Some TC Aeon questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can Psi be raised above 7 dots? Or is that more of a hard limit on how powerful subquantum powers really are?<br /> 2. Can 7 dot powers be combined? I mean, in the way normal powers can be combined by multiple psions. If all eight proxies linked, that would be some epic stuff!<br /> 3. Can biotech gain Flux diseases?<br /> 4. Non-Corrupted Aberrants, such as those inhabiting Eden. Should I use TC Aberrant, or the rules given for Aeon-Era Corrupted monstrosities? It seems to me the rules for the kind of Aberrants psions face is more intended for, to use TC Aberrant terms, Transcendence 10+ novas.<br /> 5. Aberrant Corruption \u2018weakens\u2019 Doyen just by being nearby. How should I best reflect this, in game terms? I have an idea the higher the Corruption, the harder a Doyen gets hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T15:47:41-07:00","id":1490940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490911#post1490911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Can the Detection Mega-Edge sense subquantum, the way psions can detect Quantum (\u201cCorruption\u201d)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;-9 VANISHING&quot; entry on page 165 of Aberrant indicates Novas cannot perceive things at the sub-quantum level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T15:50:23-07:00","id":1490942,"title":"","content":"Ah! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T16:00:18-07:00","id":1490945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490932#post1490932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some TC Aeon questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can Psi be raised above 7 dots? Or is that more of a hard limit on how powerful subquantum powers really are?<br /> 2. Can 7 dot powers be combined? I mean, in the way normal powers can be combined by multiple psions. If all eight proxies linked, that would be some epic stuff!<br /> 3. Can biotech gain Flux diseases?<br /> 4. Non-Corrupted Aberrants, such as those inhabiting Eden. Should I use TC Aberrant, or the rules given for Aeon-Era Corrupted monstrosities? It seems to me the rules for the kind of Aberrants psions face is more intended for, to use TC Aberrant terms, Transcendence 10+ novas.<br /> 5. Aberrant Corruption \u2018weakens\u2019 Doyen just by being nearby. How should I best reflect this, in game terms? I have an idea the higher the Corruption, the harder a Doyen gets hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>1). Human psions cannot go above 7 while psiads cannot go above 6. If Psi 8+ is possible, it'll either be in alien species or the far future of humanity.<br /> <br /> 2). No reason why they can't. Even just a single Proxy teamed up with one or two weaker psions can produce incredible effects. I did some number crunching, and I believe a completely reasonably build for the Vitakinetic Proxy, teamed up with a Psi 4 Vitakinetic and any Teleporter, basically lets them give a huge number of people at once about 13+ scale 2 soft armor, which lets them survive practically anything short of a nuclear bomb. This could help explain how the aberrant attack on Australia was defeated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3). Possibly.<br /> <br /> 4). The Aeon rules are meant to use for NPC antagonists and allies. For your campaign, use whichever set of rules let you most easily tell the story you want.<br /> <br /> 5). Everything tends to boil down to either increased Difficulty or added Complications. Boosting the Difficulty is easier, but Complications could include thematic consequences like lost psi points or injury conditions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T16:05:53-07:00","id":1490947,"title":"","content":"What sort of Complications? Could Psi Dysfunction be a viable one? Yes, I know Dysfunction is caused by imbalance among an Aptitude\u2019s Modes, but still...it <i>could</i> be used to represent the Doyen\u2019s thinking becoming impaired, couldn\u2019t it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-21-2022, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T16:47:37-07:00","id":1490950,"title":"","content":"The problem with using psi dysfunction as a complication is that it makes one of your aptitudes stronger, and it seems implausible for a Doyen to get stronger due to exposure to an aberrant. Complications could include -1 (or more) to effective psi level when determining power duration, losing an additional psi point, a headache that imposes +1 Difficulty to Intellect rolls, physical disorientation that imposes +1 Difficulty to Dexterity rolls, an injury from quantum energy &quot;poisoning&quot; the Doyen, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T16:58:04-07:00","id":1490952,"title":"","content":"Ah, missed that bit! Ok!<br /> <br /> Some TC Aeon questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are Doyen still capable of reproduction, or are they doomed to slow extinction?<br /> 2. Have Doyen ships or biotech (outside the Aeon Corebook) been described? If so, where can I find it?<br /> 3. Has it ever been revealed the identity of the low-powered Aberrant in Coalition captivity?<br /> 4. Who is The Colony, in your campaigns? I do not mean canonically, I mean in actual Storyguided games. (My personal pet theory\u2019s he\u2019s Anibal Buendia. Eufiber could be parasitic, you know. Whether it canonically can be or not is unclear.)<br /> <br /> Some TC Aberrant questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Considering that several Edges grant nova-tech and/or Q-tech, I take it that\u2019s meant to represent how ubiquitous this stuff is? The idea Divis Mal has Q-tech is rather interesting, while the notion Geryon might be packing Q-tech weaponry is <i>terrifying</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-21-2022, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T17:29:40-07:00","id":1490955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490952#post1490952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, missed that bit! Ok!<br /> <br /> Some TC Aeon questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are Doyen still capable of reproduction, or are they doomed to slow extinction?<br /> 2. Have Doyen ships or biotech (outside the Aeon Corebook) been described? If so, where can I find it?<br /> 3. Has it ever been revealed the identity of the low-powered Aberrant in Coalition captivity?<br /> 4. Who is The Colony, in your campaigns? I do not mean canonically, I mean in actual Storyguided games. (My personal pet theory\u2019s he\u2019s Anibal Buendia. Eufiber could be parasitic, you know. Whether it canonically can be or not is unclear.)<br /> <br /> Some TC Aberrant questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Considering that several Edges grant nova-tech and/or Q-tech, I take it that\u2019s meant to represent how ubiquitous this stuff is? The idea Divis Mal has Q-tech is rather interesting, while the notion Geryon might be packing Q-tech weaponry is <i>terrifying</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes and Yes. Under Alien Suns have a lot about Doyen if you want to know more.<br /> 2. Not much. As above.<br /> 3. No idea. I guess no\u2026<br /> 4. I like the Buendias Theory, but I prefer to think on a Mega Social Nova. I may try to describe the original powers he had in my head canon.<br /> <br /> 1. I need to point that Nova Tech is also amazing and pretty powerful, specially because you can have soooo many of them\u2026 anyway, to me Nova Tech and Q Tech is absolutely common to find among Novas, uncommon among non nova specialists and rare among the rest of the population. While Coretech is pretty common all around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T18:17:57-07:00","id":1490960,"title":"","content":"You know, now that I think about it, Divis Mal probably used Q-tech to initiate the Nova Age. He\u2019s old enough to have invented such things without the work of others paving the way for him. I\u2019m pretty sure Geryon doesn\u2019t have Q-tech, but the idea of him wielding a Q-tech powermaul is too delicious to let go by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T19:36:05-07:00","id":1490962,"title":"","content":"Some generic questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can novas and psions use Inspired Science? Or is that restricted to Talents?<br /> 2. Can what Talents do be detected by either novas or psions for what it is? Or are they blind to such Gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T20:17:49-07:00","id":1490963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490960#post1490960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, now that I think about it, Divis Mal probably used Q-tech to initiate the Nova Age. He\u2019s old enough to have invented such things without the work of others paving the way for him. I\u2019m pretty sure Geryon doesn\u2019t have Q-tech, but the idea of him wielding a Q-tech powermaul is too delicious to let go by.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 273 of Aberrant has artwork showing Divis Mal using a device of some sort to trigger the Nova Age. He'd apparently been working on it for decades, trying over and over again until he built one powerful enough to affect the entire world. I believe he's also responsible for causing several senior Terat members to erupt in the years before the Galatea explosion.<br /> <br /> It isn't canon, but given that Cestus Pax was secretly a full nova rather than a stalwart before the Galatea explosion, I suspect his empowerment event was because his family's car was near wherever Divis Mal was secretly conducting quantum generator experiments at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T20:30:08-07:00","id":1490964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490962#post1490962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some generic questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can novas and psions use Inspired Science? Or is that restricted to Talents?<br /> 2. Can what Talents do be detected by either novas or psions for what it is? Or are they blind to such Gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>1). IIRC there are three broad levels of super science: tech+, weird tech, and super tech. Tech+ can be used by anyone and can be made by anyone once reverse engineered. Weird tech can be used by anyone, but can only be made by Inspired, and Inspired of the wrong type take penalties to reverse engineering. Super tech can only be used or reverse engineered by the same sort of Inspired that made the super tech.<br /> <br /> 2). I believe a tiny sidebar in Adventure! indicates it is almost impossible to detect a Talent using their powers. Mega-Mental novas may be able to notice Talents succeed a statistically improbable percent of the time, and the Clairvoyant Proxy in Aeon knows some rare individuals have unusually complex interactions with probability, but barring a specific homebrew power or Edge, I doubt novas or psions have any chance of noticing anything less blatant than Dramatic Editing, and they'd probably only notice that on a legendary success (ie. Difficulty 5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T01:48:27-07:00","id":1490972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1490932#post1490932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Can Psi be raised above 7 dots? Or is that more of a hard limit on how powerful subquantum powers really are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard cap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Can 7 dot powers be combined? I mean, in the way normal powers can be combined by multiple psions. If all eight proxies linked, that would be some epic stuff! </div> </div> </div>Probably. The SG would need to do some work as I have no idea what the effects would look like, but it\u2019d be impressive!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Can biotech gain Flux diseases? </div> </div> </div>Not something we\u2019ve covered yet, but my view is yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Non-Corrupted Aberrants, such as those inhabiting Eden. Should I use TC Aberrant, or the rules given for Aeon-Era Corrupted monstrosities? It seems to me the rules for the kind of Aberrants psions face is more intended for, to use TC Aberrant terms, Transcendence 10+ novas. </div> </div> </div>What are you using them for? Player\u2019s characters - I\u2019d suggest adapting Aberrant\u2019s rules. SG characters - use Aeon\u2019s rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Aberrant Corruption \u2018weakens\u2019 Doyen just by being nearby. How should I best reflect this, in game terms? I have an idea the higher the Corruption, the harder a Doyen gets hit. </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head, their rolls gain Complication equal to the highest Quantum rating nearby, or maybe half Quantum, rounded up. Doyen takes an Injury Condition if they fail to buy off the Complication. This won\u2019t kill them but can disrupt them into an \u2018unconscious\u2019 state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T02:00:22-07:00","id":1490973,"title":"","content":"1. There are 3 leves of super science, as Shepherdboi said, the names are:<br /> - Advanced: Anyone can create, including normal people and Assassins. That is called Core Tech in Aberrant.<br /> - Inspired: Any Inspired (including Novas, Psions, etc) can create and anyone can use, but each inspired kind have their own inspired super science related to their powers. That is called Nova Tech in Aberrant and Inspired Biotech in Aeon. While biotech must be formated, the kind that has powers and neutrals can use is Inspired.<br /> - Powered: Only Novas and Psions/Psiads can create and use, and only their own kind, because it interact with their powers. That is called Q-Tech in Aberrant and Powered Biotech in Aeon. This tech give the user powers, and cant be activated by themselves.<br /> <br /> 2. Like for Psi detection by Quantum its up to the SG, but the general answer is no.<br /> - A Nova can sense other Novas, but would not be capable of differentiate Psiads and Talents from baselines.<br /> - A Psiad can detect Novas and Psiad but cant differentiateTalents from Neutrals .<br /> - A Talent can detect all kind of powers and identify them with the proper Gift (a Cunning gift, See the Halo or something like that, I dont have the book here).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T02:09:47-07:00","id":1490974,"title":"","content":"Expanding on the idea of Novas x Aberrant antagonists.<br /> If you have both books available, I suggest to use the rules in Aeon to create your adversaries, you may call them different names, but its far simpler to create powered NPCs as described in Aeon than as in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> Not: I use Aeon rules for Nova adversaries for simplicity in Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-22-2022, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T09:46:59-07:00","id":1491005,"title":"","content":"Thanks! You\u2019ve all been super helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T11:41:42-07:00","id":1491014,"title":"","content":"A couple of TC Aberrant questions:<br /> <br /> 1. How do I simulate the old 1e Bodymorph power? I know the simplest answer is the Dormancy Edge, but what about other options? My thought is a Power Suite, but I\u2019m not sure. Is Molecular Chameleon re-skinned with slightly different Tags what I\u2019m looking for? EDIT: I just re-read Transformation. Maybe that with some negative Power Tags, to whittle the shapeshifting options down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-22-2022, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:33:13-07:00","id":1491022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491014#post1491014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of TC Aberrant questions:<br /> <br /> 1. How do I simulate the old 1e Bodymorph power? I know the simplest answer is the Dormancy Edge, but what about other options? My thought is a Power Suite, but I\u2019m not sure. Is Molecular Chameleon re-skinned with slightly different Tags what I\u2019m looking for? EDIT: I just re-read Transformation. Maybe that with some negative Power Tags, to whittle the shapeshifting options down?</div> </div> </div> </div>Add Restricted tags to the power that can be used only in the Bodymorph form (based in a power), and to those that are all linked to eachother.<br /> <br /> That is the suggestion in my Houserules: Quantum in my signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T13:01:29-07:00","id":1491028,"title":"","content":"I like this notion. It\u2019s far simpler than anything <i>I\u2019d</i> have thought up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T13:25:34-07:00","id":1491036,"title":"","content":"TC Aberrant power system is effect based, in opposition to Psi system and Gift systems that are focused in the way they do and not what is the result.<br /> <br /> Usually the easiest way to simulate any power is to list the effects you want and build your power around them, with tags to adjust them to what you intend.<br /> <br /> There are many exceptions in the available effects and some of the powers suggested in other books are very precisely covering aspects, like pocket universes, replicating objects, and other things like that.<br /> <br /> But as a system TC Aberrant is pretty solid in many ways. I think we take advantage of the experience the designer have with M&amp;M (that is fantastically solid for a D20 game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T15:58:11-07:00","id":1491051,"title":"","content":"Some TC Aberrant questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Should Transformations reflect powers? Or a theme? Like, \u201cthis nova is aquatic, and be becomes more and more fishlike\u201d, or \u201cthis nova is hyper-aggressive, so his Transformations follow suit\u201d. Or would they be more random? I\u2019m of the opinion they, like powers, should follow a coherent theme.<br /> 2. A question concerning the Quantum Agent power: could it be modeled as a suit of \u2018power-armor\u2019, not Q-tech, but rather something he conjures purely out of Quantum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T16:16:11-07:00","id":1491054,"title":"","content":"1. No but they can, and usually do because usually they have some \u201cside effects\u201d. 2. Yes, you could create an agent big enough to be around you for sure. But it would not be the best way to model the best way to model a quantum powered armor created from pure quantum. My suggestion is to go and use the powers you want your armor to have to create a power suit with many techniques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T17:14:53-07:00","id":1491056,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> Some TC Adventure! questions....<br /> <br /> 1. What is the different, if any, between a daredevil and a Talent?<br /> 2. I\u2019ve seen conflicting information, so... Are locations affected by Flux, the way the Inspired are? 1e (which I adore) had some pretty strange locales in it. And, if so, do they fade away as the Hammersmith Event runs out of steam?<br /> 3. I know TC Aether already covers this, but, from a TC Adventure! standpoint, would Frankenstein\u2019s Monster best be represented by stalwart rules?<br /> 4. How far away from Earth did the Hammersmith Event affect? I know the Doyen sensed it and moved quickly erect their barrier, but did the Telluric wave create weird things on Mars or Venus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T18:20:08-07:00","id":1491061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491051#post1491051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. A question concerning the Quantum Agent power: could it be modeled as a suit of \u2018power-armor\u2019, not Q-tech, but rather something he conjures purely out of Quantum?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want a summoned minion that looks like a guy in armor (or a robot), use Quantum Agent with the Agent Theme: Machine. This gives you a minion that obeys your orders and has powers of its own.<br /> <br /> If you want your character to summon armor that they wear, use Quantum Field and just have the forcefield look like armor as a special effect. If the &quot;armor&quot; grants additional powers, just buy those powers and limit them to only working while Quantum Field is active.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T18:33:31-07:00","id":1491064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491056#post1491056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> Some TC Adventure! questions....<br /> <br /> 1. What is the different, if any, between a daredevil and a Talent?<br /> 2. I\u2019ve seen conflicting information, so... Are locations affected by Flux, the way the Inspired are? 1e (which I adore) had some pretty strange locales in it. And, if so, do they fade away as the Hammersmith Event runs out of steam?<br /> 3. I know TC Aether already covers this, but, from a TC Adventure! standpoint, would Frankenstein\u2019s Monster best be represented by stalwart rules?<br /> 4. How far away from Earth did the Hammersmith Event affect? I know the Doyen sensed it and moved quickly erect their barrier, but did the Telluric wave create weird things on Mars or Venus?</div> </div> </div> </div>1). They're the same thing, although Daredevil Gifts lean more towards a high risks=high rewards paradigm.<br /> <br /> 2). Strange Places do seem to be tied to flux, and a lot of them do appear to fade over time.<br /> <br /> 3). It depends on if Frank is a PC or an NPC, and what books you're using. NPCs generally get condensed write-ups unless they're major characters, in which case you should stat them up using whatever book is most convenient. In Aether, it is probably easiest to stat him as a Magog. In Adventure!, he'd be built as a stalwart. Aberrant would likely represent him as a weak nova. Aeon could stat him as a Superior.<br /> <br /> 4). Not sure how much was effected, but the Doyen must have used precognition since the &quot;blanketing&quot; happened so fast that only Mercer, Bhurano, and Donighal got the full effect; people in the same room as them had their powers shackled. This leads me to suspect that, whatever the Doyen did, it was already in place, waiting to be triggered by (and fueled by) the Hammersmith Event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T18:39:57-07:00","id":1491065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491061#post1491061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a summoned minion that looks like a guy in armor (or a robot), use Quantum Agent with the Agent Theme: Machine. This gives you a minion that obeys your orders and has powers of its own.<br /> <br /> If you want your character to summon armor that they wear, use Quantum Field and just have the forcefield look like armor as a special effect. If the &amp;quot;armor&amp;quot; grants additional powers, just buy those powers and limit them to only working while Quantum Field is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! This has been incredibly informative. More questions in the near future...<br /> <br /> Actually, I have one right now, for TC Aberrant...<br /> <br /> 1. Can a Power Suite be attached to a Mega-Attribute?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T19:02:44-07:00","id":1491068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491065#post1491065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! This has been incredibly informative. More questions in the near future...<br /> <br /> Actually, I have one right now, for TC Aberrant...<br /> <br /> 1. Can a Power Suite be attached to a Mega-Attribute?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically no, although there are ways around this. A few examples:<br /> <br /> 1). For the aforementioned Quantum Field armor, if you want your character's forcefield to act as a strength magnifying exoskeleton, you don't need a power suite, you just need to buy Mega-Might with the negative Tag &quot;only while Quantum Field is active&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2). If you want variable physical Mega-Attributes, buy Transformation with the negative Tag &quot;only grants physical Mega-Attributes&quot;.<br /> <br /> 3). If you want various Mega-Attributes, but don't want to be limited to physical enhancement, go with Boost. A sample build:<br /> <br /> Boost 3: Intellect (Tag: Duration, Tag: Extra Attribute: Resolve, Tag: Extra Attribute: Composure).<br /> This gives you three extra dots in Intellect, Resolve, and Composure. If this takes any of them over 5, the extra dots become Mega-Attributes.<br /> <br /> Now buy Technique: [Boost 3: Might (Tag: Duration, Tag: Extra Attribute: Dexterity, Tag: Extra Attribute: Cunning)].<br /> This gives you three extra dots in Might, Dexterity, and Cunning. If this takes any of them over 5, the extra dots become Mega-Attributes.<br /> <br /> Now buy Technique: [Boost 4: Presence (Tag: Duration, Tag: Extra Attribute: Manipulation)].<br /> This gives you <b>four</b> extra dots in Presence and Manipulation. If this takes either of them over 5, the extra dots become Mega-Attributes.<br /> <br /> You've just made a Mega-Attribute boosting power suite without using Technique on any Mega-Attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T00:12:15-07:00","id":1491081,"title":"","content":"As I read now <b>TC </b><b>Adventure!</b> myself\u2026 Generally \u2013 what <b>Shepardboi</b> written, only\u2026 I advise to read <b>TC Aether</b> preview if you can \u2013 it answer a lot of questions for next era in timeline after it, the <b>Adventure!</b> precisely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491056#post1491056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I\u2019ve seen conflicting information, so... Are locations affected by Flux, the way the Inspired are? 1e (which I adore) had some pretty strange locales in it. And, if so, do they fade away as the Hammersmith Event runs out of steam?</div> </div> </div> </div>In <b>Aether</b>, it\u2019s assumed that using <i>Aether</i> energy let to open gates to various dimensions. Aether could you do truly impossible stuff with it \u2013 over the top even for Flux from where it\u2019s coming \u2013 but changes of Aether are not permanent if not sustained by Aether. It may even takes years to Unwind it on itself \u2013 but it will Unwind. So all Strange Places in <b>Adventure!</b> that were open in Aether times simply slide to nothingness, year by year. Hammersmith Event could reinvigorate few of them for a decade or two \u2013 but nature of Aether is Unwind, in the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491056#post1491056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I know TC Aether already covers this, but, from a TC Adventure! standpoint, would Frankenstein\u2019s Monster best be represented by stalwart rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would still work with Aether rules \u2013 they seems more adequate for more monstrous Gogs and especially for Magogs ( that are directly monster-like ) \u2013 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1489736-tc-aether-clarification-squire-gog-magog\">see more here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491056#post1491056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. How far away from Earth did the Hammersmith Event affect? I know the Doyen sensed it and moved quickly erect their barrier, but did the Telluric wave create weird things on Mars or Venus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Limit only it as much as you need, story-wise? I would simply allow my Players to sail to Mars if they build Aparatus, boat and everything. \ud83d\ude0e You can also make that they open in reality AetherGate and jump into<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Carter_of_Mars\" target=\"_blank\"> other reality Mars \u2013 that has Green, Red, Yellow and White Martians</a>\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T08:12:19-07:00","id":1491093,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I appreciate it, guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T08:53:45-07:00","id":1491094,"title":"","content":"Some TC Aeon questions, concerning the mini-sourcebook I bought with 30-some odd Psychic Edges:<br /> <br /> 1. How relatively common do you imagine Psychic Edges like these are? Some are rather niche.<br /> 2. Do you imagine this sort of research is perpetually ongoing? In my games, yes it is. <i>But</i>, only SOME of them are in common use. The new Quantakinesis Psychic Edges, for instance, have yet to be invented<br /> 3. Is it feasible to have Proxy Tier Psychic Edges? Like, I don\u2019t know, using a 7-dot Psychic Edge to bioengineer a semi-sentient pet? I know vanishingly few psions would have such powers, but still...<br /> 4. Can 6-dot powers work with Psychic Edges? I don\u2019t mean the base power the Psychic Edge alters, but rather the altered power, itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T09:09:52-07:00","id":1491096,"title":"","content":"A comment on the weird places and things, they are not caused by Hammersmith, they happen &quot;naturally&quot; on remote places where none goes for a long time and they may appear and disappear at any time. Atlants for example is in the botton of the ocean during Aether and Adventure eras.<br /> <br /> This kind of stuff also allow some esoteric items to work, those items are basically super science items, but with no &quot;scientific approach&quot;. A psion can create a biotech that helps him to see the future, but a esoteric item would be a deck of cards, or some other &quot;magical item&quot;.<br /> <br /> As far as we know, most of the weird places vanished before Nova era, but you may find some of them in the most remote places, like a savage valley in Antartica with dinosaurs and a worm rain forrest, or an iland in the middle of the ocean that is always covered by clouds, or a cave in the botton of the sea from where a giant monster emmerges once in a while.<br /> <br /> Edit: Adding, there are still weird things happening even durng Aeon era, so it can be a really interesting game if you wanto to explore those weirdplaces at any age as you wish.<br /> <br /> I imagine Aegis era world will be covered by weird places, as most of it was barelly touched by humans. It would be fun to have natural philosophers discussing the nature of the weird places that they once in a while may find, while other times ate not there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-23-2022, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T09:16:34-07:00","id":1491097,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Maybe a Mediterranean island inhabited by a low-Quantum nova \u201cwitch\u201d and the pig sub-Aberrant mutants she makes out of hapless sailors!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T09:21:33-07:00","id":1491098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491094#post1491094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some TC Aeon questions, concerning the mini-sourcebook I bought with 30-some odd Psychic Edges:<br /> <br /> 1. How relatively common do you imagine Psychic Edges like these are? Some are rather niche.<br /> 2. Do you imagine this sort of research is perpetually ongoing? In my games, yes it is. <i>But</i>, only SOME of them are in common use. The new Quantakinesis Psychic Edges, for instance, have yet to be invented<br /> 3. Is it feasible to have Proxy Tier Psychic Edges? Like, I don\u2019t know, using a 7-dot Psychic Edge to bioengineer a semi-sentient pet? I know vanishingly few psions would have such powers, but still...<br /> 4. Can 6-dot powers work with Psychic Edges? I don\u2019t mean the base power the Psychic Edge alters, but rather the altered power, itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>This book is not official book, but a Community Content, but its a good one for sure.<br /> My oppinion:<br /> 1. As we have many thousands of psions, I am quite sure there are lots of them.<br /> 2. I believe most of them surge naturally as they learn they can do (basically you can do many many different things, any psion with the proper mode dots can do all that is described in those edges paying extra psi and having some complications in the rolls, but those that buy the edges just can do it easier)<br /> 3. Why not? But instead they are actually unique powers that only proxiy level psions can create and teach to other proxy level psions. Check Prometheus Unbound for the proper rules.<br /> 4. In tesis yes, because those are just tricks they learnd to do with the powers, and so can grow with the powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T09:22:20-07:00","id":1491099,"title":"","content":"Would I be correct in that Transformation Quantum power with the Impose Only Tag and one or more applications of the Duration Power Tag is the best way to implement \u201csub-Aberrant mutants\u201d in the Nova Age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T09:54:39-07:00","id":1491101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491099#post1491099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would I be correct in that Transformation Quantum power with the Impose Only Tag and one or more applications of the Duration Power Tag is the best way to implement \u201csub-Aberrant mutants\u201d in the Nova Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. I believe the best way is by using powers that cause Flux on the target, like Healing, or by using a tag you create to do that.<br /> The point of the Sub-Aberrant is not to be transformed by a power, that would be temporary, but the character be deformed until become something other than human by exposure to quantum energies.<br /> <br /> But yes, you could create temporary subaberrants (powerful ones by the way) using transformation and Impose Only tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T10:48:42-07:00","id":1491103,"title":"","content":"So, a tag designed for that, just for the Healing power? Hmmm. Interesting.<br /> <br /> A TC Aeon question:<br /> <br /> 1. How many psions can potentially link their powers noetically? I don\u2019t seem to be able to find a hard limit. If, say, enough Upeo wa Macho joined into a single use of Transportal, could they reach the Andromeda Galaxy?<br /> <br /> A TC Aberrant question:<br /> <br /> 1. How far <i>can</i> you go, with the optional Goliath rules? Like, if a Galactus stand-in came to Earth, how absurd could I get while staying within the letter of the rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T10:52:51-07:00","id":1491105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491096#post1491096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine Aegis era world will be covered by weird places, as most of it was barelly touched by humans. It would be fun to have natural philosophers discussing the nature of the weird places that they once in a while may find, while other times ate not there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine Dinosaur Valley showing in <b>Adventure!</b> - that as you run through it - you got out on one of <b>Aegis</b> islands?! \ud83d\ude0e And then characters in the <b>Modern / Core Trinity</b> find your 1930s remains in excavations site of 3000-4000 years old settlement, with dino bones added to mix?! \ud83d\ude2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T11:06:44-07:00","id":1491107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491103#post1491103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a tag designed for that, just for the Healing power? Hmmm. Interesting.<br /> <br /> A TC Aeon question:<br /> <br /> 1. How many psions can potentially link their powers noetically? I don\u2019t seem to be able to find a hard limit. If, say, enough Upeo wa Macho joined into a single use of Transportal, could they reach the Andromeda Galaxy?<br /> <br /> A TC Aberrant question:<br /> <br /> 1. How far <i>can</i> you go, with the optional Goliath rules? Like, if a Galactus stand-in came to Earth, how absurd could I get while staying within the letter of the rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Healling have the side effect of causing 1 Flux after 10 successes used on the same character in 24h. My suggestion is to create a &quot;Corrupt&quot; tag that grants 1 Flux to the target of the power as a sideeffect.<br /> <br /> Aeon 1. As many as you want, but it can raise the combined Psi up to 5 or 7 if any Proxy tier psions among them. So, no Andromeda for you...<br /> <br /> Aberrant 1. As far as you wish. The idea of the system is to allow you to defeat a enemy without necessarily a direct combat. How you kill galactus is another question and it may be an entire chanlenge appart after taking him out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T11:42:30-07:00","id":1491110,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I am EXTREMELY grateful to all of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T13:24:03-07:00","id":1491117,"title":"","content":"A TC Aeon question:<br /> <br /> 1. We have the following aliens:<br /> Aberrants (technically!);<br /> Bullseye Entities (sadly, extinct);<br /> the Coalition (HR Giger would be proud);<br /> Chromatics;<br /> the Doyen;<br /> the Qin.<br /> Do any other species exist, or is this the official list? I know Martians are a species in TC Aether, but do they endure <i>past</i> TC Aether?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T14:09:32-07:00","id":1491123,"title":"","content":"We have playable:<br /> - Aberrants (TC Aberrant)<br /> - Coallition (some phyles at least, Under Aliens Skies)<br /> - Chromatics (UAS)<br /> - Qin (Distant Worlds)<br /> - Listeners (UAS)<br /> - Gardeners (kind of, worth the read, UAS)<br /> <br /> Besides those we have a few other aliens and stranger things around in Under Alien Skies and Distant Worlds. If you like aliens (real aliens, not human with heavy makeup), those two books are amazing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T14:38:53-07:00","id":1491126,"title":"","content":"What\u2019re Listeners? What are Gardeners?<br /> <br /> And yes, I prefer my aliens <i>alien</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:01:18-07:00","id":1491136,"title":"","content":"If you want the truly incomprehensible type of alien then there is The Breach.<br /> <br /> All of them are in &quot;Under Alien Skies&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:09:00-07:00","id":1491137,"title":"","content":"Oooo! \u2018The Breach\u2019! Sounds Cthulhu-y!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:31:43-07:00","id":1491141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491103#post1491103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A TC Aeon question:<br /> <br /> 1. How many psions can potentially link their powers noetically? I don\u2019t seem to be able to find a hard limit. If, say, enough Upeo wa Macho joined into a single use of Transportal, could they reach the Andromeda Galaxy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Noetic links are kind of self limiting. It doesn't matter if you're linking two psions or 1000, the base benefit is +1 die/+2 dice if you're linked to a proxy, and everyone must pay 1 psi point every time anyone activates a power. The real benefit is the page 208 perk, and I believe even those only apply once each. If five vitakinetics are linked, whoever is acting gets Enhancement to powers used against living creatures equal to the psi trait of whichever other vitakinetic has the highest psi.<br /> <br /> So if your character is in a noetic link with psions of each Aptitude, each with Psi 5, they get +1 die to the dice pool and as many of the page 208 bonuses as apply to that specific power use, but everyone pays 1 psi point or the power fails.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491103#post1491103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A TC Aberrant question:<br /> <br /> 1. How far <i>can</i> you go, with the optional Goliath rules? Like, if a Galactus stand-in came to Earth, how absurd could I get while staying within the letter of the rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Goliath rules can be pushed so far that you can easily adapt them to non-combat encounters. Want to defeat an international corporation or tyrannical dictatorship? Treat it like a Goliath. Are you trying to win a political campaign or save the city from an unnatural disaster? Treat it like a Goliath. This is like performing a complex action with multiple milestones, except the situation you're resolving can (and probably will) fight back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:34:13-07:00","id":1491142,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll be using the Goliath rules for cosmic-scope entities beyond even novas, and kaiju.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:53:26-07:00","id":1491145,"title":"","content":"A TC Aeon question:<br /> <br /> 1. Can Technokinesis 5 affect Q-tech? Would it be possible, and, if so, would the psion in question suffer a penalty of some sort, like an Injury or a Condition, appropriate to the Q-tech in question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T19:29:00-07:00","id":1491150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491145#post1491145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A TC Aeon question:<br /> <br /> 1. Can Technokinesis 5 affect Q-tech? Would it be possible, and, if so, would the psion in question suffer a penalty of some sort, like an Injury or a Condition, appropriate to the Q-tech in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Technokinesis 5 interferes with devices, it may manage that much against Q-Tech, provided the Q-tech actually runs on electricity (as noted in the first sentence of the Technokinesis entry, before any of the listed powers), although the attempt may incur a higher Difficulty or a minor Complication.<br /> <br /> Of course, since Q-Tech needs to be attuned to the user, Technokinesis wouldn't work properly at outright controlling the device since a psion can't attune to a quantum device. I believe there is a Talent Gift that allows them to make Q-Tech work for one single use, but Gifts aren't fundamentally opposed to quantum the way psi is opposed to quantum.<br /> <br /> If the Q-Tech device includes any sort of electronics or computer programming, a psion may be able to use Technokinesis 2-4 to turn the device off or temporarily scramble the programming, but (again) the attempt may incur a higher Difficulty or a minor Complication.<br /> <br /> If you decide on an increased Difficulty, you may consider figuring the Difficulty normally, them add half the device's Rank. My justification would be that, the higher the device's Rank, the more the quantum nature of the device interferes with the psi power. In that case, the psion would be best served by using the lowest level power available, since they'd gain the most Enhancement to their roll that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:06:22-07:00","id":1491206,"title":"","content":"A reverse of the above question:<br /> <br /> 1. Could a nova with the Digital Scan Mega-Edge detect something Alex Cassel uses Subquantum Computing (Electrokinesis 7) on? My thought is no, as subquantum is too \u2018small\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:19:46-07:00","id":1491210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491206#post1491206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A reverse of the above question:<br /> <br /> 1. Could a nova with the Digital Scan Mega-Edge detect something Alex Cassel uses Subquantum Computing (Electrokinesis 7) on? My thought is no, as subquantum is too \u2018small\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is No, because as it says its Subquantum and so out of reach for Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:37:33-07:00","id":1491216,"title":"","content":"I figured as much. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T12:10:26-07:00","id":1491796,"title":"","content":"A TC Aberrant question:<br /> <br /> 1. How old <i>can</i> novas get? I\u2019ve seen some material saying 150 years all the way up a millennia or more.<br /> 2. What were the Doyen doing, during the Nova Age, besides shitting themselves in absolute panic? They <i>had</i> to sense N-Day, and the shattering of their barrier...<br /> 3. What is the difference between reaching Transcendence 10 as opposed to Quantum 10? As I figure it, Transcendence 10 turns you into a bodyhorror nightmare without increasing your power, but Quantum 10 doesn\u2019t necessarily mutate you, \u201cjust\u201d turning you into a god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-29-2022, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T12:31:04-07:00","id":1491798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491796#post1491796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A TC Aberrant question:<br /> <br /> 1. How old <i>can</i> novas get? I\u2019ve seen some material saying 150 years all the way up a millennia or more.<br /> 2. What were the Doyen doing, during the Nova Age, besides shitting themselves in absolute panic? They <i>had</i> to sense N-Day, and the shattering of their barrier...<br /> 3. What is the difference between reaching Transcendence 10 as opposed to Quantum 10? As I figure it, Transcendence 10 turns you into a bodyhorror nightmare without increasing your power, but Quantum 10 doesn\u2019t necessarily mutate you, \u201cjust\u201d turning you into a god?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Depends on Mega Stamina, but they can become immortal.<br /> 2. Probably doing other things and maybe trying to infiltrate Earth to prevent Novas to grow too powerful.<br /> 3. Transcendence 10 you become something that is not human, Quantum 10 you become too powerful to be in the universe.<br /> Notice that Transcendence 10 doesnt means deformed monster, just means the Nova dont care about being human and dont care much about humans, sou they just stop being human, psychologically or physically (or both). Quantum 10 means your power is just too much, like a Type 2 civilization of a single person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T12:36:56-07:00","id":1491800,"title":"","content":"Ah, ok!<br /> <br /> So....is Antaeus reaching Transcendence 10, then? In the little comic book you can read from the main Onyx Path frontpage, Antaeus seems....unconcerned...for the fate of humanity, valuing ecosystems as a whole above individual lives. It seems sociopathic, yet his love for Earth\u2019s ecosystems is also genuine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T13:00:21-07:00","id":1491805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491800#post1491800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, ok!<br /> <br /> So....is Antaeus reaching Transcendence 10, then? In the little comic book you can read from the main Onyx Path frontpage, Antaeus seems....unconcerned...for the fate of humanity, valuing ecosystems as a whole above individual lives. It seems sociopathic, yet his love for Earth\u2019s ecosystems is also genuine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! My favorite example would be Dr Manhattan turning more and more distant until decided to just go away to explore space and live in Mars. He just don't care anymore, don't care if he is alone, think people is boring and go away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T14:23:34-07:00","id":1491815,"title":"","content":"Since TC Aberrant did away with the sterilization bullshit:<br /> <br /> 1. Are the children of two novas born baseline, with unexpressed M-R coils, born a nova, or what?<br /> 2. Is the gene for the M-R coils dominant or recessive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T07:40:55-07:00","id":1491903,"title":"","content":"Here's another bunch of statements that lead to a couple of questions. I'm going to leave out Aether (because I need to re-read it) and Anima (because I missed the KS and am waiting for the release to grab it). Please correct me where I'm wrong. <br /> <br /> The statements-<br /> * It seems like Talents just sort of happen. Events like the Hammersmith experiment in 1922 and Bhurano's experiments in 2104 &quot;activated&quot; more Talents, but they seem to just naturally happen. Being at ground zero of the Hammersmith event caused Max Mercer to become a &quot;Mega Talent&quot; (for lack of a better term). <br /> * Psychic powers seem to require activation. Hammersmith's event caused more latents to become psiads/mesmerists (and made Bhurano a &quot;Mega Psiad&quot;), and later SK's experiments created a bunch of latents and a few rare psiads. But it took the Prometheus Chambers to create full-blown psions (though psions' powers are capped because the Doyen are jerks). <br /> * Similarly, Novas need to be activated. Hammersmith created Dr Primoris and activated Stalwarts. Later Primoris/Mal created more novas. <br /> * That said, Cestus Pax seems to have naturally erupted. <br /> * The Doyen put something in place after Hammersmith to prevent novas from occurring, but Mal blew it up.<br /> * Stalwarts (now called Superiors) can be activated in the Aeon era, but it requires special science to make it happen. <br /> <br /> So here are the questions: <br /> * Prior to Tesla, were there psiads and stalwarts? Presumably they were super-rare. There were also rare Gogs and Magogs (who, like Dracula, are not exactly novas or even Aberrant mutants, but sort of their own thing). <br /> * Similarly, were there new (obviously super-rare) psiads and stalwarts manifesting between Adventure and Aeon? We know that some pre-existing mesmerists, stalwarts (and even Gogs and Magogs) have extended lifespans and are thus still creeping around. <br /> * Are there (also super rare) &quot;natural&quot; stalwarts in the Aeon era?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2222-rickjonzz","name":"RickJonzz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2222_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T08:27:54-07:00","id":1491907,"title":"","content":"All of your statements are almost true.<br /> <br /> Talents, Psiads and Stalwarts (the low powered Novas) can all just appear with some triggering effect.<br /> Talents are far easier, while Psiads and stalwarts are rarer (far rarer).<br /> Hammersmith made it easier to people to become Talents, Stalwarts and Psiads, and Mal and Bhurano did too, but focused in different directions, Mal to Quantum and Bhurano to Psi.<br /> Bhurano was not a Super Psiad, she was a powerful Psiad, but far less powerful than she was as a Proxy. Same for Mal, he was a nova, but a weak one (far more powerful than stalwarts, but still a weak nova).<br /> Novas can happen naturally but they are even rarer than Stalwarts before N-Day, and become the only form of human quantum user after it.<br /> <br /> On the questions:<br /> * There were Psiads and Stalwarts manifesting for millennia (maybe) before N-Day, including Adventure and Aether.<br /> * There were Psiads and Novas manifesting between Aberrant and Aeon<br /> * Mal N-Day event unlocked the human quantum powers, basically turning all possible Stalwarts into Novas. At least for a while, no more stalwarts. The novas erupted between Aberrant War and before Bhurano event were almost all corrupt because they erupted in QFZ, but after that there may be more \u201cclean\u201d novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-30-2022, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T08:28:20-07:00","id":1491908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491903#post1491903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another bunch of statements that lead to a couple of questions. I'm going to leave out Aether (because I need to re-read it) and Anima (because I missed the KS and am waiting for the release to grab it). Please correct me where I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> The statements-<br /> * It seems like Talents just sort of happen. Events like the Hammersmith experiment in 1922 and Bhurano's experiments in 2104 &quot;activated&quot; more Talents, but they seem to just naturally happen. Being at ground zero of the Hammersmith event caused Max Mercer to become a &quot;Mega Talent&quot; (for lack of a better term).<br /> * Psychic powers seem to require activation. Hammersmith's event caused more latents to become psiads/mesmerists (and made Bhurano a &quot;Mega Psiad&quot;), and later SK's experiments created a bunch of latents and a few rare psiads. But it took the Prometheus Chambers to create full-blown psions (though psions' powers are capped because the Doyen are jerks).<br /> * Similarly, Novas need to be activated. Hammersmith created Dr Primoris and activated Stalwarts. Later Primoris/Mal created more novas.<br /> * That said, Cestus Pax seems to have naturally erupted.<br /> * The Doyen put something in place after Hammersmith to prevent novas from occurring, but Mal blew it up.<br /> * Stalwarts (now called Superiors) can be activated in the Aeon era, but it requires special science to make it happen.<br /> <br /> So here are the questions:<br /> * Prior to Tesla, were there psiads and stalwarts? Presumably they were super-rare. There were also rare Gogs and Magogs (who, like Dracula, are not exactly novas or even Aberrant mutants, but sort of their own thing).<br /> * Similarly, were there new (obviously super-rare) psiads and stalwarts manifesting between Adventure and Aeon? We know that some pre-existing mesmerists, stalwarts (and even Gogs and Magogs) have extended lifespans and are thus still creeping around.<br /> * Are there (also super rare) &quot;natural&quot; stalwarts in the Aeon era?<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Cestus Pax seemingly became a full-on Nova while the Doyen Barrier was still intact, and the core members of the Teragen were also full-on Novas before the Doyen Barrier fell due to Divis Mal's experiments in forced Nova eruptions, my personal Cestus Pax theory is that his car was passing by whatever secret lair Divis Mal was using at the time, and he got caught near the edge of one of those experiments. Alternately, he was near a powerful flux event that spewed enough quantum energy into the area to briefly overcome the Doyen Barrier.<br /> <br /> Stalwarts and Superiors are also not the same thing. Stalwarts happened naturally while Superiors are what happen when scientists carefully cause and cripple a Nova eruption at the same time.<br /> <br /> As for your questions:<br /> <br /> 1). Psiads and novas can occur whenever someone is exposed to sufficient noetic or quantum energy, so a flux event that spews one of those energies into the environment could cause an appropriate reaction. These people would presumably be more powerful than those empowered during the Adventure! era since they came into their power before the Doyen Barrier was put into place.<br /> <br /> 2). There were definitely a few rare mesmerist and stalwart manifestations between those eras. Flux events kept happening; the Doyen Barrier just kept the fallout on a local level while making it much harder for them to increase their underlying power level.<br /> <br /> 3). Anyone empowered by quantum energy during the Aeon era presumably gets pumped up to Nova/Aberrant level.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T08:44:19-07:00","id":1491910,"title":"","content":"On Pax and the Terragem, Mal was working on N-Day for a long time, its perfectly possible all Novas (including himself, maybe) were to be Stalwarts that erupted by accident or intentionally into Novas (or were Stalwarts that were turned into Novas) due to lower scale experiments of Mal.<br /> <br /> Pax could be just passing by a few kilometer away from Mal the time he was testing his machine and become a Nova.<br /> <br /> It's not canon, but possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-30-2022, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T09:27:37-07:00","id":1491914,"title":"","content":"Thanks all. I'm poking at doing a Planetary-style game in the Aeon era, and wanted to be sure I was connecting the dots on my conspiracy board correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2222-rickjonzz","name":"RickJonzz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2222_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T10:58:55-07:00","id":1491924,"title":"","content":"1. Is TC Assassins a full on Era? Can it be considered its own \u2018corebook\u2019? Or is it just an expansion for the central rulebook?<br /> 2. What\u2019re the character types? Talents, I\u2019d assume, but I\u2019d like to know before I make my purchase?<br /> 3. Does it have information on assassins in the Nova Age?<br /> 4. Does it have lots of setting lore? Lots of new factions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T11:21:05-07:00","id":1491928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491924#post1491924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is TC Assassins a full on Era? Can it be considered its own \u2018corebook\u2019? Or is it just an expansion for the central rulebook?<br /> 2. What\u2019re the character types? Talents, I\u2019d assume, but I\u2019d like to know before I make my purchase?<br /> 3. Does it have information on assassins in the Nova Age?<br /> 4. Does it have lots of setting lore? Lots of new factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No. Its a rules/set expanssion that can be used in basically any point of the timeline with little changes, but its focused in the Core setting.<br /> 2. They are basically Talents, but they are aware of their abilities and their Masteries (basically the same as Gifts, but more focused) have a strong connection with hunting and killing people.<br /> 3. No, but it wont change much to Nova Age. Aeon and Adventure is harder to say and may work a bit different.<br /> 4. It has a lot of Factions and have a lot of lore about the world we dont see in the action stories of regular Talents. It's all about shadow and twilight, the places and games regular people stay away for their own safety, like the world of the assassins from Wanted, John Wick and Kill Bill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T11:45:06-07:00","id":1491930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491928#post1491928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. No. Its a rules/set expanssion that can be used in basically any point of the timeline with little changes, but its focused in the Core setting.<br /> 2. They are basically Talents, but they are aware of their abilities and their Masteries (basically the same as Gifts, but more focused) have a strong connection with hunting and killing people.<br /> 3. No, but it wont change much to Nova Age. Aeon and Adventure is harder to say and may work a bit different.<br /> 4. It has a lot of Factions and have a lot of lore about the world we dont see in the action stories of regular Talents. It's all about shadow and twilight, the places and games regular people stay away for their own safety, like the world of the assassins from Wanted, John Wick and Kill Bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T11:51:47-07:00","id":1491931,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Is it about the same size as TC Aeon and TC Aberrant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T12:03:45-07:00","id":1491933,"title":"","content":"It's 188 pages long, while Core is 233, Aberrant is 314 and Aeon is 385.<br /> <br /> To be fair, it is dense in content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T12:15:14-07:00","id":1491935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491903#post1491903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another bunch of statements that lead to a couple of questions. I'm going to leave out Aether (because I need to re-read it) and Anima (because I missed the KS and am waiting for the release to grab it). Please correct me where I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> The statements-<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding the books - you are generally correct. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491903#post1491903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Prior to Tesla, were there psiads and stalwarts? Presumably they were super-rare. There were also rare Gogs and Magogs (who, like Dracula, are not exactly novas or even Aberrant mutants, but sort of their own thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>In my own ( maybe a bit noncanon ) take, <b>Gogs and Magogs are general previouse takes on Inspired, before Hammersmith</b> - so Psiads/Stalwarts/Mesmerists can ALL be Gogs and Magogs.<br /> <br /> Also - <b>if you look Psiads before Aether, even Hammersmith - look for the 'Mystics' of various magical traditions around the world.</b> \ud83d\ude0e In my own game I just started just after Hammersmith, my players are looking in India for various Psiads and Max Mercers as literal 'avatars of Khali' - by vision from Three Prongs mystic. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491903#post1491903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Similarly, were there new (obviously super-rare) psiads and stalwarts manifesting between Adventure and Aeon?</div> </div> </div> </div>See above, but can be also a bit more scientific with each decade goes on. Also, see our <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1487200-trinity-fan-era-cosmic-minds-psi-in-1950s-70s\">fan miniera about Psi in 1950s-70s</a>. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491903#post1491903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Are there (also super rare) &quot;natural&quot; stalwarts in the Aeon era?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that is the case. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T12:31:40-07:00","id":1491939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491928#post1491928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's all about shadow and twilight, the places and games regular people stay away for their own safety, like the world of the assassins from Wanted, John Wick and Kill Bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>... And<b> Assassin's Creed</b> frenchise - 3 of 5 core Societies in <b>TC Assassins</b> are based loosely on <b>AC </b>groups. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> How to fan marry <b>TC Assassin</b>s with <b>AC</b> games backstory - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1483116-assassin-s-creed-in-tc-assasins?p=1490579#post1490579\">more in this topic</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T14:52:49-07:00","id":1491952,"title":"","content":"Has anyone done stats Writeup on big characters in the Nova Age? 1e and the d20 versions are acceptable, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T16:00:19-07:00","id":1491956,"title":"","content":"A few nitpicks: <br /> <br /> 1. Superiors aren't stalwarts. They're an artificially imposed variant of quantum empowerment that's not as powerful as Novas, but which also lacks the tendency to mutate into something only nominally human. <br /> 2. Novas <i>are</i> stalwarts \u2014 or rather, stalwarts are what Novas look like under the constraints oof the Doyen Barrier. Unlike the original Adventure!, Stalwarts have, in theory and somewhat in practice, access to the full range of Quantum Powers, including such things as being able to fly and fire blasts of energy; they're just more limited in their ability to do so (for instance, the flight only lasts for a few turns). That said, stalwarts aren't immune to the mutating effects of channeling Quantum, in the form of Telluric Burnout. Dr. Primorus and Cestus Pax are Novas in the sense that they're individuals who are more powerful than your average stalwart. <br /> 3. The naturally occurring Psi-empowered come in two basic types: those with innate power, and those with innate channeling. Psiads are what you get when these coexist; Latents are what you get when there's innate channeling but not innate power. Psions are what you get when you start with a Latent and artificially stimulate their power. (That implies a third type of naturally occurring Psi-empowered individual: one with power but no channeling; it's been suggested that such individuals would have full access to all bio-tech as if they were a psion, but wouldn't have any psionic powers of their own.) <br /> 4. Mesmerists are psiads in the same way that stalwarts are Novas. <br /> 5. Squires (\u00c6ther) are daredevils (Adventure!) are Talents. The relationship between daredevils or Squires and Talents is the <i>opposite</i> of the relationship between stalwarts and Novas: the unique environments found in the \u00c6ther and Adventure! ages <i>empower</i> them, making Dramatic Editing even easier than it is in other eras. <br /> 6. Gogs and Magogs <i>are not</i> psiads and Novas. They are <i>\u00c6ther-enhanced Talents</i>. They either channel \u00c6ther through Apparatus (Gogs) or through their body, resulting in mutations (Magogs). Magogs <i>are not</i> Quantum-powered, despite some superficial resemblances between them and Novas. <br /> 7. Psiads and Novas can appear in any era (though in Adventure!, they manifest as stalwarts and mesmerists); but outside of Adventure!, Aberrant, and \u00c6on (so far), they're rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T16:13:10-07:00","id":1491957,"title":"","content":"Had any stalwarts survived to N-Day, would they\u2019ve stayed stalwarts, or undergone a full eruption? Would a mesmerism upgrade to a psiad?<br /> <br /> And what happened to Hammersmith, himself? He received more Z-waves than even <i>Divis Mal</i>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-30-2022, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T16:25:22-07:00","id":1491958,"title":"","content":"All Stalwarts that existed on N-Day Erupted. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that it was necessarily a <i>big</i> Eruption; Dark Stars are a thing in Aberrant, after all, and a Dark Star is, essentially, a stalwart \u2014 just using the Nova rules instead of the Talent rules. So a stalwart can \u201cErupt\u201d and effectively remain unchanged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T18:24:34-07:00","id":1491966,"title":"","content":"What do you, in your own campaigns, had happened to Hammersmith, himself? Dude was closer to the machine than anyone else, soaked up more Z-waves than <i>Divis Mal</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T18:39:32-07:00","id":1491968,"title":"","content":"He was killed by the explosion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T18:59:58-07:00","id":1491969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1491968#post1491968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was killed by the explosion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T19:01:10-07:00","id":1491970,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T23:30:11-07:00","id":1491981,"title":"","content":"Stalwarts don't necessarily become novas. Stalwarts are their own thing.<br /> <br /> But yes, Hammersmith died in the explosion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T00:19:58-07:00","id":1491984,"title":"","content":"Ok! Thanks, guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T00:28:06-07:00","id":1491987,"title":"","content":"My understand of Stalwarts is that they are what Novas would be if not by Mal work.<br /> They are more stable in terms of Flux, gaining temporary transformations that vanish with rest, but far less powerful.<br /> <br /> I made a house rule for Stalwarts using Quantum rules, and I put them as Tier 2 (TN 8) and limited to Q3, but immune to their own production of Flux (external sources still accumulate as it does for Baselines).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T10:40:25-07:00","id":1492016,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d use what\u2019s in TC Adventure!, personally. I feel reinventing the wheel can be unnecessary, sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T10:42:20-07:00","id":1492018,"title":"","content":"A TC Aether question:<br /> <br /> 1. Do any Gogs or Magogs survive into later Eras? Because the idea of Dracula meeting Otha Herzog is just too tempting to <i>not</i> use!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T14:00:24-07:00","id":1492032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1492018#post1492018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A TC Aether question:<br /> <br /> 1. Do any Gogs or Magogs survive into later Eras? Because the idea of Dracula meeting Otha Herzog is just too tempting to <i>not</i> use!</div> </div> </div> </div>Adventure! characters do encounter the undead, some of which may be Magogs, and at least a few Magogs survive until the Nova age and pass themselves off as Novas.<br /> <br /> Gogs would have a harder time becoming unaging since none of their Gifts have permanent effects. A super old Gog would either need to invent a Gift that makes the user younger whenever it is used, or find some other path to eternal life (ie. the fountain of youth, peaches of immortality, Olympian ambrosia, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 08-31-2022, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T14:04:41-07:00","id":1492033,"title":"","content":"Canonically? Coooool. Which ones? My dream of Otha Herzog meeting Vlad Tepes might now be possible!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or Antaeus running into Frankenstein\u2019s monster!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-31-2022, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T15:25:20-07:00","id":1492040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1492033#post1492033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically? Coooool. Which ones? My dream of Otha Herzog meeting Vlad Tepes might now be possible!</div> </div> </div> </div>No names were given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T15:26:15-07:00","id":1492041,"title":"","content":"Power-wise, how does a Magog stack up against a nova?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Plus, a few more questions.<br /> <br /> 1. How many of you have homebrewed your own aliens, especially for TC Aeon?<br /> 2. Has anyone posted character write ups, if not here, then elsewhere online? Edition is irrelevant...for the most part. Era is unimportant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-31-2022, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T18:15:35-07:00","id":1492056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1492041#post1492041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power-wise, how does a Magog stack up against a nova?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Plus, a few more questions.<br /> <br /> 1. How many of you have homebrewed your own aliens, especially for TC Aeon?<br /> 2. Has anyone posted character write ups, if not here, then elsewhere online? Edition is irrelevant...for the most part. Era is unimportant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other people can comment more comprehensively about Magogs, but the vibe I got was somewhere between Stalwart and Nova. A lot of their Gifts give them access to some Scale, and some Mega-Edge type effect, but they broadly lacked access to things like Nova powers. It's been a bit since I read Adventure but mechanically they felt a bit like Stalwarts+.<br /> <br /> I'm getting ready to run an Aeon game focused on an exploratory jumpship, so I've been thinking about making new aliens but haven't gotten that far in planning yet. Focused on wrapping up my Scion game and then taking a few months off to play in games and plan for Aeon in more detail. I'll post if I make any new aliens!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> has a thread where he has made some antagonists using the system for making PC's for a game he is planning, and statted some of the Adventure era Storyguide Characters as starting characters.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_32938/StoryPath-Nexus?page=1&amp;sort=6a&amp;include_community_content=1&amp;show_only_community_content=1\" target=\"_blank\">Storypath Nexus</a> on drivethrurpg has a bunch of fan made stuff, usually for a couple of bucks. There are two Teambooks for Aberrant, some characters made for games at conventions, and I think a Psion strike team or something. Onyx Path also has a cheap supplement or two with pre-made characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":". 08-31-2022, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T18:21:33-07:00","id":1492058,"title":"","content":"Thank you! Time to go a\u2019huntin\u2019....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T21:08:26-07:00","id":1492067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1492041#post1492041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Has anyone posted character write ups, if not here, then elsewhere online? Edition is irrelevant...for the most part. Era is unimportant.</div> </div> </div> </div>My NPCs write-ups:<br /> 1. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1489201-tc-major-npcs-stats-across-eras?p=1489214#post1489214\">Fan take on <b>Max Mercer</b> </a>for 2E <b>Adventure!</b>, just after Hammersmith Event and his return to world ( circa 1923 ).<br /> I use mainly <b>TC Core</b> and <b>Adventure</b> manuscript - but used a bit of <b>Aether</b> to fill in his life gaps, as it's just start of <b>Adventure!</b> era. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> [ I need him for my own game. Will end it in few days now. ]<br /> 2. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1478161-character-creation-for-tc-2e\"><b>Ferdinand 'Franz' Herz</b></a> - Thule/Nazis Mesmerist villian for 2E Adventure! [ Also will end him in couple of days, as I need Franz for adventure. \ud83d\ude0e ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-01-2022, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T15:36:35-07:00","id":1492123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1492041#post1492041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power-wise, how does a Magog stack up against a nova?</div> </div> </div> </div>PC Novas get 150 xp at character generation while Magogs get four Gifts and three points to spread among their Facets, so Novas are meant to be much more powerful than Magogs in theory. In practice a tricked out Magog can stomp on a Nova in a very limited subset of abilities after a mere four sessions, and get even scarier after that since Facets cost 10 xp and Gifts cost 5 xp while Quantum costs 16 xp and Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, and Powers cost 12 xp.<br /> <br /> A Magog with 135 xp (which is less than a Nova starts with) has maxed all three Facets and taken all seven of the Gifts that boost Scale by the appropriate Facet. That gives the Magog Scale 6 to Durability, Might (lifting strength only), leadership rolls, mental rolls, mental speed, physical speed, and Magog Gifts where Power Scale is relevant.<br /> <br /> The biggest limits on a Magog's powers are the fact that Aether's Gift word count is split between three character types while Aberrant is dedicated entirely to Novas, and most of the really good Magog Gifts require the character to take a new deviation. The first limitation isn't too bad since you can easily invent new Gifts, and the second doesn't have to be crippling if you choose the right deviations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T16:14:15-07:00","id":1492126,"title":"","content":"XP is not the best measure in this case. Magogs can increase their scale much faster than Novas. Sure, Novas start better, but if you put them evolving side by side, 150 xp after you will have Magog far more powerful than a Nova.<br /> <br /> For example, to reach scale 6 in all scales (power, might, durability, body speed, mind speed, mental and social) need the initial package and 150 xp (135 xp for the 4 facets and 15 for gifts).<br /> A nova need many many more, mainly because they don\u2019t increase scale as a simple thing, they increase aspects of that. Basically they need 5 dots in 6 mega attributes and 5 or 6 dots in mega edges, that total 400+ XP.<br /> <br /> Magog power grow is too fast to compare to anything. I personally would limit it to half facet instead of full facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-01-2022, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T19:13:11-07:00","id":1492128,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Interesting. I like the Magogs being much more narrowly focused, but in some ways stronger than novas, and weaker in other ways. There\u2019s a kind of symmetry, there.<br /> <br /> Is transcending to a godlike state possible for Magogs? When novas reach Quantum 10, they become basically omnipotent, albeit no longer concerned with the pettiness of mortalkind, irregardless if they\u2019re human or alien. Can Magogs reach a similar kind of deityhood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T10:24:12-07:00","id":1492172,"title":"","content":"A few more questions:<br /> TC Aeon:<br /> 1. Is humanity the only species so far to have the potential for Inspiration, Quantum powers <i>and</i> Psi? I can see why the Doyen are so worried about us.<br /> 2. How many alien civilizations\u2019re under Doyen control? The TC Aeon Corebook reveals one such species, but there must be others, right?<br /> 3. Am I correct in my assumption the Doyen were the most powerful species, til Aberrants invaded the wider galaxy? I wonder: did any Aberrants reach the Doyen homeworld?<br /> <br /> TC Aberrant:<br /> 1. How viable is the idea that Quantum powers can have Powered Edges attached to them? Edges that modify powers? Or is this unnecessary, considering how tags work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-02-2022, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T11:10:49-07:00","id":1492174,"title":"","content":"For your Aberrant question, I'd say that's what tags are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T21:06:55-07:00","id":1492198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1492172#post1492172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few more questions:<br /> TC Aeon:<br /> 1. Is humanity the only species so far to have the potential for Inspiration, Quantum powers <i>and</i> Psi? I can see why the Doyen are so worried about us.<br /> 2. How many alien civilizations\u2019re under Doyen control? The TC Aeon Corebook reveals one such species, but there must be others, right?<br /> 3. Am I correct in my assumption the Doyen were the most powerful species, til Aberrants invaded the wider galaxy? I wonder: did any Aberrants reach the Doyen homeworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Talents seem to be able to arise in any species, either in species that lack the potential for quantum or psi, or for members of the species that lack those abilities. Humans are unique in that they have the potential to manipulate quantum and psi.<br /> <br /> 2. The Qin and recently the Chromatics are the only ones we know about. The Qin aren't under Doyen control so much as the Doyen just took steps to limit the development of the Qin so they'll never ascend or become a threat.<br /> <br /> 3. Most powerful is hard to quantify. The Doyen failed to ascend and are trapped, other species that ascend are probably much much more powerful than the Doyen. The Doyen are heavily driven by fear, so any species that seems like it might possibly be a threat to them tend to get destroyed. I think they're also not fans of seeing other species ascend because it reminds them of their failure. The galaxy is huge though, and there are a limited and dwindling number of Doyen so they miss things, like the Yarrans who seemingly evolved and ascended without the Doyen interfering.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Doyen are probably one of the most powerful if only because they tend to stomp on anyone who could be a threat, but they don't spend all their time checking every star in the galaxy for new threats so they miss things. <br /> <br /> If Aberrants did reach the Doyen homeworld the Doyen wouldn't have noticed, none of them have been there in 200,000 years, and Aberrants probably wouldn't have known what they were seeing if they did reach it. A totally lifeless rock with ruins millions of years old, there are more interesting places to visit. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T18:36:35-07:00","id":1492473,"title":"","content":"Well. Got both Distant Worlds <i>and</i> Under Alien Skies. Money <i>extremely</i> well spent. <br /> <br /> I <i>love</i> the Listeners! They\u2019re so adorable, yet so awesome. The Breach wasn\u2019t what I expected. I really enjoyed reading it. The Coalition chapters in both sourcebooks were <i>superb</i>. And, yes, the Doyen are indeed cosmic assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T19:24:07-07:00","id":1492476,"title":"","content":"I find the Listeners <i>utterly</i> charming. I love that they taught themselves how to speak human languages in advance of first contact, but can only speak at a yelling volume. Their extremely intricate political crime. How they're such an awkward fit as allies of humanity. Also I love that they come across as very cautious but in a very different way than the Qin, but not at all cowardly. You can see how their evolution shaped them, but also very good reasons to avoid galactic notice based on all the ruins of alien civilizations they've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T19:30:21-07:00","id":1492477,"title":"","content":"\u2018Water-stilling\u2019 is such a neat idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T23:41:18-07:00","id":1492488,"title":"","content":"One thing that I love about the Aeon setting is how aliens are, well, Aliens. Sentient beings like us, but also completely alien in body and mind. An understanding can be reached, but there will always be a serious communications barrier due to radical differences in biology and culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T05:26:53-07:00","id":1492509,"title":"","content":"Whenever reading about the Doyen before their failed ascension I always envision shuckle from pok\u00e9mon. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/image/jpeg;base64, ze5PuwDSB/GUPqcS Sf269Fgn2QlXeGv 9V9N6mwKUAHmbULIo/MRJhHBAIIIPII5BHuMti5tbl7ItNeTZERJngiIgCIiAIiIAiIgCIiAIiIAiIgCIiAIiIAiIgCInNrdUtVT2NwtaM7fBQSf5QCK7X7Sbf8ARqTtfbuuswD4KNkLtBBDO2DgHIUAs2fZV9eh0iIuF4z7TEkszt5s7nljx1PM4ezlcV7rceK533kdN7dQD5hRhBn7qLO9HnCzdV9236Xhf9NkY9T TYZiwiarbgMAkAscLkgZOCcD14BP