era of cooperation, where conflicts between them were reduced to a minimum and the operatives could count on the help and resources of other societies more freely. If they had played their cards right, they could have united and become THE society of the shadows, the secret masters of the world. Sadly, that's not how it went.<br /> <br /> The element that ultimately brought everything down was the one that brought them together in the first place: The novas. What to do with them? At the beginning, they stayed the hell away from them as much as possible due to fear of them bringing too much light into the shadow, and only ordered a hit under the most extreme circumstances. However, as the attitude towards Novas soured, contracts to take them out started to grow, same as the rewards. Societies became divided between those who wanted to keep limiting contact with Novas and those who wanted an open hunting season.<br /> <br /> The aberrant war was the deciding factor, everyone agreed that the Novas had to be dealt with, but many in the Shadow felt that going at them too openly risked extinction. In the end, personal ambition and ideology won and each society went their separate way. For some, the allure of glory or simple greed proved too much and fought the gods openly, with devastating consequences for their societies. Others chose a more indirect approach, trying to work through other organizations and weakening the support structure of the Nova rather than going after the Nova itself. Then others just tried to minimize the collateral damage and save as many people as possible. <br /> <br /> Regardless of the approach, the Shadow did what it always did, it adapted to the changing world. Societies fell or transformed into something else, a new shadow emerged with new faces but with the same grim objective. The only thing they shared in common was one simple thing: Never again. The Assassins swore that they would never again hesitate to hunt down the false gods that promised utopia but delivered hell. That's why in the future, a new breed of Assassin emerged, the Aberrant hunters, the shining knights of the world of shadows that hunted down the dragons everyone was afraid of. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>AWESOME. Consider this notion stolen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T16:36:04-07:00","id":1493221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493218#post1493218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my head cannon, the appearance of Novas shook the Shadow to its core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought this was the official view, not just your head canon. Novas were too \u2018large\u2019 and their power too great for the Shadow to remain shrouded. The presence of novas who would either associate with people from the Shadow, or turned their attention to working against people from the Shadow, just busted it open. The Shadow was basically shredded in the Aberrant era.<br /> <br /> I thought I\u2019d read that from Ian somewhere, but perhaps it was a fan thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T17:23:18-07:00","id":1493223,"title":"","content":"It wouldn\u2019t surprise me. <br /> <br /> But I can totally imagine the Swarm actively recruiting stealth-based novas, such as El Supay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T01:30:32-07:00","id":1493234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493221#post1493221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought this was the official view, not just your head canon. Novas were too \u2018large\u2019 and their power too great for the Shadow to remain shrouded. The presence of novas who would either associate with people from the Shadow, or turned their attention to working against people from the Shadow, just busted it open. The Shadow was basically shredded in the Aberrant era.<br /> <br /> I thought I\u2019d read that from Ian somewhere, but perhaps it was a fan thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if there's an official view, but this is also a perfectly valid approach. My take is based on the societies letting paranoia and distrust of the Novas be the default attitude. In another version, greed and opportunism wins over from the beginning which means societies work with, and even use, Novas. The problem is, as you said, that Novas are larger than life and the shadow struggles to contain them. Eventually, the shadow ruptures, societies are exposed to the world, and like a piece of bloody meat in a piranha tank law enforcement and rival criminal organizations turn them to shreds. It would take years or even decades after the aberrant war for a new shadow to establish itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T02:17:56-07:00","id":1493235,"title":"","content":"Your description of Shadow transformation is just awesome! Well, now its ours... (imagine the Bugs Bunny meme here)<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think the way assassins masteries work, the same way for Psiads and some overt Talents, would be interpreted by many as Nova powers, weak ones, but still novas powers. Lets say picking a bullet in the air is not something normal person can do...<br /> <br /> The tech at start of Nova era, as well as the almost complete knowledge of other sources of powers, would make them feel like Novas, as they can do impossible things. Maybe with some help of the core of Aeon Society, that have the knowledge of the different kinds of Inspired, or studding how Novas powers work they may find ways to differentiate what is a real Nova and what is not, the assassins can identify themselves and fight Novas certain they are not ones (and the following time line you described, that is now ours).<br /> <br /> It's kind of tricky to think about it, but people don't know how their powers work and dont know how other people powers work, so, unless you deal with many different powered people and have some kind of sense of source (Talents and Assassins may have it and all Psiads have it, but they may still lack the experience to differentiate them), there is no way to tell who is what.<br /> Also, the media will not help, if you can track people in the other side of the world or if you can lift a ping pong ball with your mind, you are a Nova, maybe a weak or a more secretive form of Nova, but still a Nova.<br /> We know who is who because we can see their char sheets, but the Psiads we see in the Aberrant book are all treated as Novas by the people in game including themselves, one of them is a Terat, she literally think she is a goddess because she has pychokinetic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T10:53:49-07:00","id":1493252,"title":"","content":"Who is the psychokinetic would-be Terat? I don\u2019t remember seeing it in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T11:36:32-07:00","id":1493255,"title":"","content":"My players are THE WORST - ( or I am on NPC roleplay ) - First they talk with Mercer in 1923 - they get from him that he saw 100 years into the future. \ud83d\ude2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T11:59:26-07:00","id":1493259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493252#post1493252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is the psychokinetic would-be Terat? I don\u2019t remember seeing it in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not on Core. It's on Aberrant book, one of the sample antagonists (I think the last one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:12:45-07:00","id":1493262,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Just looked her up. I like that even some Terats don\u2019t know the difference between nova and psiad. I mrean, Divis Mal probably would, but most Terats have no way of discerning between the two.<br /> <br /> Which makes me wonder: what happened to those psiads that thought they were novas? Psiads, if they\u2019re anything like psions, have extended lifespans. Did any psiads accompany Aberrants in the Aberrant Exodus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:33:10-07:00","id":1493265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493262#post1493262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes me wonder: what happened to those psiads that thought they were novas? Psiads, if they\u2019re anything like psions, have extended lifespans. Did any psiads accompany Aberrants in the Aberrant Exodus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anima mentions in passing that some of the psiads helping Dr. Bhurano investigate events in the city of Cascade have to keep a low profile because they were around during the Nova Age and would be mistaken for Aberrants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:47:32-07:00","id":1493269,"title":"","content":"Yeah. When will TC Anima be out? Anybody know? Or TC Adventure!, for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:51:06-07:00","id":1493270,"title":"","content":"I would number the Psiads in a hundred and something during Nova era, maybe a little more. Could even say, but I know some people will disagree, that N-Day helped many Psiads to get their powers, if not for a &quot;Telluric&quot; help (after all, the N-Day device is a reengineered version of Hammersmith, maybe there is some Noetic reinforcement too), for letting them to try their powers thinking they were Novas.<br /> <br /> For what they did during and after Aberrant War, I guess many went away with the Novas, theinking themselves as Novas, but as they are not detected by quantum detectors and had no transformations, they were free to walk around undetected, as lonk they kept their powers on secret (Sarah as example).<br /> <br /> There is one other relevant psiad family that I would like to point out in Mission Statements that is probably around for a while doing shadowy stuff, named Rousseau... She seams to be around since Aberrant 1e... and they did stay on Earth and made a lot of money after the war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-18-2022, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T13:14:33-07:00","id":1493271,"title":"","content":"Ooooh! Sophia! Is she still around, in TC Aeon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T13:15:42-07:00","id":1493272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493221#post1493221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought this was the official view, not just your head canon. Novas were too \u2018large\u2019 and their power too great for the Shadow to remain shrouded. The presence of novas who would either associate with people from the Shadow, or turned their attention to working against people from the Shadow, just busted it open. The Shadow was basically shredded in the Aberrant era.<br /> <br /> I thought I\u2019d read that from Ian somewhere, but perhaps it was a fan thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I mentioned on the Discord, I think. It's not canon in the sense that it's in any published material, but that's my take on it, at least. There's no way for Assassins to remain long in Shadow in a world with novas. Everywhere they go, the spotlight follows. Every step they take, quantum ripples shred the delicate veil propped up to keep Assassins from view.<br /> <br /> Of course, once the Aberrant War is over, there's no reason that new Societies couldn't form...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493269#post1493269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Yeah. When will TC Anima be out? Anybody know? Or TC Adventure!, for that matter.<br /> </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> Onyx Path doesn't do release dates, but you can track the progress of Adventure! and Anima in the monthly Kickstarter updates, or on the monthly <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/release-roundup-august-2022\" target=\"_blank\">Release Roundup blog posts</a>, or look at any weekly changes in the Monday Meeting Notes blog.</span> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T13:18:00-07:00","id":1493274,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Ian!<br /> <br /> And yeah, I agree, novas should have shattered the Shadow. I imagine El Supay found his way to the Shadow side of things with some incredible ease!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T13:52:36-07:00","id":1493280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493271#post1493271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooooh! Sophia! Is she still around, in TC Aeon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Sophia, but her Daughter (or maybe grand daughter), Colette, is alive during Aeon era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T14:09:11-07:00","id":1493282,"title":"","content":"Is Colette a psiad or a psion?<br /> <br /> If a psion, What Aptitude? What Psi order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T14:23:11-07:00","id":1493285,"title":"","content":"I think Colette is a psiad. I believe she\u2019s found in Mission Statements under Hounds of the Void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T14:31:01-07:00","id":1493286,"title":"","content":"About rebuilding Assassins Societies after Aberrant War - Didn't Anima era/book have Assassins-like Allegiance in it? At least I remember the hackers collective that is legacy of Les Fantomes from TC Core modern era?<br /> <br /> Do we have Allegiance of Daylight or MegaCorp in Anima or Aeon eras related with Morocco? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-18-2022, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T14:31:45-07:00","id":1493287,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Other than the obvious (Aeon Society NPCs, major Aberrants, etc), what other TC Aberrant-era characters get mentioned in TC Aeon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T19:09:45-07:00","id":1493299,"title":"","content":"I think Vladimir Sierka gets mentioned in Terra Firma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T02:08:07-07:00","id":1493311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493272#post1493272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I mentioned on the Discord, I think. It's not canon in the sense that it's in any published material, but that's my take on it, at least. </div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for confirming it was said somewhere. I didn\u2019t think I\u2019d just made that up. \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T02:44:08-07:00","id":1493312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493286#post1493286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About rebuilding Assassins Societies after Aberrant War - Didn't Anima era/book have Assassins-like Allegiance in it? At least I remember the hackers collective that is legacy of Les Fantomes from TC Core modern era?<br /> <br /> Do we have Allegiance of Daylight or MegaCorp in Anima or Aeon eras related with Morocco? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Les Phantomes is an alliance of thieves, not assassins. No assassins societies were mentioned in Anima as far as I know.<br /> 2. I'm not sure, I would have to check the books.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding rebuilding the shadow after the aberrant war, here's my take on it.<br /> <br /> First, it will take years or even decades as I said before, the shadow is not a phenomenon that can be rebuilt in the short term. During this time, new assassins would emerge bit by bit, then as their numbers increase they would create new societies, rebuild old ones from the ground, or even find the ones that hid and help them get back on their feet.<br /> <br /> Speaking of old societies, we need to establish what happened to them:<br /> <br /> DAUGHTERS OF THE JACOBINS: Destroyed. Sorry, but I just don't see how could they have survived. During the war, they would have thrown caution to the wind trying to save as many people as possible, even if that brought the attention of the aberrants who would eventually destroy them. <br /> THE KRUGU VOROV: Survived, you don't become THE criminal masterminds without being clever, but they do as a shadow (pardon the punt) of their former selves. The destruction of organized crime on a global scale and the damage of the aberrant war weakened them too much, forcing them to hide in Russia and wait for better times. <br /> THE SIGNAL: Survived, they took some heavy hits, but their decentralized nature played in their favor by making it impossible to target their leadership. In fact, I would go as far as to say that the signal is the only society who managed to stay active after the war and even leading the new shadow. The Shanghai accords would change that, sadly.<br /> SOCIETY OF LEONIDAS: Destroyed, like the king of the spartans and the 300 they went to a battle they KNEW they couldn't win, but that wasn't the point. They sacrificed themselves to show the rest of the assassins that the aberrants could be fought. They died in a blaze of glory and with a smile in their faces.<br /> THE SWARM: Destroyed, pride comes before the fall and greed makes for a poor advisor. They tried to play everyone in the name of profit and power and paid the price. By the time the Aberrants went after them, they found themselves weakened and without allies. Future Assassins talk about the swarm as a cautionary tale.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T03:03:46-07:00","id":1493314,"title":"","content":"My view is slightly different. The societies of assassins would be largely destroyed but the heads are not that easy to put down, and they would adapt to the new condition.<br /> <br /> Daughters of The Jacobins would be destroyed during the war, with a few remaining members becoming the new Aberrant Hunters society.<br /> KV as you said, they are the masterminds of the shadow, if only one society fits the shrink shadow, its them.<br /> Signal is largely unchanged, if not empowered by the decentralized and the war. They would adapt fast to the new shrink shadow, probably extend out of it, working as elites and soldiers of fortune, embracing the possible status of Novas to certain extend.<br /> SoL is tricky, they would be destroyed as a society, but all they built over the years would be absorbed, probably by the shadowed part of Aeon (Protheus, Minerva, Babel Dossier, Polyphemus, etc).<br /> Swarm would bend with the twilight and the daylight societies it have connections, remaining greatly powerful as much as possible. Afterall the Swarm was made to be an shadow extend of those, not the opposite, its their business and one that will always be needed.<br /> <br /> My view of Aberrant war is less about Us v. Them and more Shit hit the Fan. Humans and Novas would fight for each side, the war was not an open war with teams of novas fighting against arms, it was a guerrilla, with novas and countries being attacked and attacking in retaliation. There was no start of the war, it was a growing conflict that started sometime in &quot;present day&quot; as minor thing and scaled up until the ultimatum.<br /> <br /> Even the idea of all novas going crazy feels more like propaganda than anything. Sure, there was a lot of crazy novas, and each one is as powerful as a small country, but there were a lot of novas doing nothing and following their lives until they were kicked out of Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-19-2022, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T03:25:57-07:00","id":1493315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493312#post1493312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DAUGHTERS OF THE JACOBINS: Destroyed. Sorry, but I just don't see how could they have survived. During the war, they would have thrown caution to the wind trying to save as many people as possible, even if that brought the attention of the aberrants who would eventually destroy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that DAUGHTERS are probably destroyed after 'Novas exposure'- but remaining Assassins from them come to darker parts of Aeon Society, maybe as Aberrant Hunters in <i>Project Proteus</i>. Remember that DAUGHTERS have already very close relations with Aeon from the start of both - and <i>Aeon Group</i> is not so ideal shinning diamond in <b>Anima</b> and <b>Aeon</b> eras...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T05:27:02-07:00","id":1493322,"title":"","content":"Just a clarification, when I say that a society is destroyed, I don't necessarily mean that it's completely eradicated. It is expected for some members and resources to survive and move on, especially if those members belong to the leadership of the society.<br /> <br /> The majority of survivors from the daughters of the Jacobins and the society of Le\u00f3nidas would have joined project Protect Proteus in AEON as some of you pointed out, with a few joining the signal, going independent or retiring. The remains of the Swarm would have probably become some sort of private security corporation; that said, taking into account that their base is in Japa...sorry, I meant Nippon, it wouldn't surprise me if the government didn't do something similar to the yakuza and reach some sort of agreement with them, becoming Nippon's secret army of ninja assassins (Why also ninjas? Well, I think ninjas are cool ;P).<br /> <br /> The aberrant war was indeed a huge mess, with no clear lines or sides. This is precisely one of the main reasons why the combined efforts of the Assassin societies could not have stopped it. There was no clear army leader or ruler they could kill that would have ended the conflict, instead there were hundreds of them, each with their own plans.<br /> <br /> Now, how about we speculate a bit about the situation of the surviving assassin societies in Anima, I will also come with two new ones later:<br /> <br /> <b>The Signal:</b> Since they survived the Nova age and the Aberrant war with few loses, they've become one of the dominant assassin societies of the world. I imagine them like deadsec from the watch dogs video games, a crypto-insurgency army that uses a lot of AI technology and with Assassins with an uncanny ability to use hacking for their hits. However, with their growth I think they would have expanded their operations and also become like the Archangel alliance.<br /> <br /> <b>The Krugu Vorov: </b>This society was humbled by the Novas. Such a situation can't be tolerated ever again. After entrenching their position in Russia and becoming its indisputable masters, they started to slowly rebuild their global criminal empire, with an emphasis on controlling weapon trafficking, especially if they include Nova Tech. They've become obsessed with acquiring the most lethal weapons in the world to make sure that when the Novas come back, it will be the last thing they ever do.<br /> <br /> <b>Mure \u200b\u7fa4\u308c:</b> This society is how I see the evolution of the Swarm. They reorganized as a cross between a private security agency, a ninja clan, and an intelligence agency supervised by the Nippon government. They're the eyes and ears (and sometimes the knife) of Nippon on the world they've left behind, making sure that Nippon, and then the world, stay safe. Their operatives have access to the most advanced cybernetics in the planet. (Cyber ninjas, even cooler than regular ninjas)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 09-19-2022, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T05:53:21-07:00","id":1493324,"title":"","content":"Swarm becoming the secret army of Nihon government is great. And add to it cybernetics and Superiors and you have an awesome setting for internal/international politics and intelligence in a secrete war...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T08:12:59-07:00","id":1493330,"title":"","content":"Oo! Oo! Nihonjin Assassins vs psion infiltrators!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T08:43:40-07:00","id":1493332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493324#post1493324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarm becoming the secret army of Nihon government is great. And add to it cybernetics and Superiors and you have an awesome setting for internal/international politics and intelligence in a secrete war...</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Superiors as Assassins is...risky. I don't think Nippon would take this path. It all comes down to control, and you want to make sure that you can control your army of super assassins. With Cybernetics, you can ensure that you're the only one with the means to repair and give more implants to the Assassins, and if they go rogue? Well, you can turn them off or tell them to self-destruct. Superiors though? Their power is their own, you can't take it away or give more. Also, some superiors may start to question their servitude and think that perhaps they should do some cleaning in the Nippon government...perhaps even take over, for the good of Nippon of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T09:11:29-07:00","id":1493334,"title":"","content":"I wonder how Divis Mal or Max Mercer would react to Superiors. With Mal, it\u2019s probably be outrage, but what would Max think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T09:18:32-07:00","id":1493335,"title":"","content":"Superiors are not used as Assassins, they are a different set of tools, hypercapable in other things (maybe also in killing, but...).<br /> <br /> Superiors are exactly as you are describing the assassins, all Superiors working for the government have some cybernetics, including the kill switch, and are selected among the most dedicated and stable members of the society that are naturally capable of becoming superiors. They are the best tool and the most guarded secret of Nihon government.<br /> <br /> In the end, to best fit the politic game and create some kind of inner adversary in Nihon, the idea may be the Swarm becoming the ninjas working for the corporations inside Nihon, and fighting a secret war against the government for information and control over the technology. The government with talents and Superiors x the corporations with talents and assassins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T11:19:58-07:00","id":1493343,"title":"","content":"What are Superiors? Weaker version of Novas from Japan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T11:33:33-07:00","id":1493345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493343#post1493343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Superiors? Weaker version of Novas from Japan?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are basically Novas that had their eruption controled in certain way.<br /> They can improve their bodies and minds beyond human levels, but not as high as Novas, and cant use quantum powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T14:18:08-07:00","id":1493355,"title":"","content":"Neutered novas, basically. Nihonjin scientists found a way to detect unerupted novas, and then pinpoint which ones were likely to gain <i>really</i> large levels of Transformations; these unerupted novas have a treatment performed where their potential as novas is <i>severely</i> curtailed. Which is why I\u2019m damn curious how Divis Mal and Max Mercer would feel about the idea. (The Taniwe, for instance, treat Superiors as if they were cripples.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-19-2022, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T15:23:35-07:00","id":1493358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493355#post1493355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neutered novas, basically. Nihonjin scientists found a way to detect unerupted novas, and then pinpoint which ones were likely to gain <i>really</i> large levels of Transformations; these unerupted novas have a treatment performed where their potential as novas is <i>severely</i> curtailed. Which is why I\u2019m damn curious how Divis Mal and Max Mercer would feel about the idea. (The Taniwe, for instance, treat Superiors as if they were cripples.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not exactly true. The scientists dont pick the ones that will not become aberrants, because its about life choices and not genetic definitions, what they pick is the kids that are the most loyal and psychologically stable and allow them to chose if they want to serve their country for the rest of their lives to their country. Those that reject or are rejected receive a genetic treatment that removes all chances to become a Nova or a Psion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T16:35:55-07:00","id":1493436,"title":"","content":"Some TC Assassins questions:<br /> 1. Would it be possible for an Assassin to work for a Talent faction? Like, an Assassin working for ultimate combat Mastery for the Transcendent Alliance?<br /> 2. The \u2018sudden surge\u2019 in the Assassin population in 1922 was caused by the Hammersmith Event, wasn\u2019t it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T18:33:36-07:00","id":1493445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493436#post1493436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some TC Assassins questions:<br /> 1. Would it be possible for an Assassin to work for a Talent faction? Like, an Assassin working for ultimate combat Mastery for the Transcendent Alliance?<br /> 2. The \u2018sudden surge\u2019 in the Assassin population in 1922 was caused by the Hammersmith Event, wasn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Sure<br /> 2. Yes. That\u2019s also about the time the Worshipful Company of Killers was destroyed too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T04:24:24-07:00","id":1493468,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I just came up with two new assassin societies for our hypothetical future shadow in Anima, let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> <b>Terra Sanguin\u00e1ria:</b> Terra Verde wasn't always the group of heroic rogues that we saw in AEON. Decades before, when it was just beginning, it was more a coalition of different groups that shared the same overarching goal, and some of those groups were a bit too eager and bloodthirsty. However, as the organization grew and consolidated their position, the more...let's just say &quot;extreme&quot; members had to be &quot;removed&quot;. To the surprise of everyone involved, most of them left when asked. The truth was that many knew already that they were no longer welcome in Terra Verde, and so they went ahead and created a new Terra, one that had their same thirst of blood for those who saw the planet as nothing more than a resource to be exploited.<br /> The group would have never survived had their leaders not been talents, some of them survivors from the destruction of the previous shadow, who saw the organization as a means to regain power. Terra Sanguinaria is an ecoterrorist group, but one that shies away from the usual bombings and public profile of terrorist groups in favor of discreet surgical strikes with their assassins and indirect manipulation. They're the secret masters of most criminal organizations in the Southern Hemisphere, and bitter rivals with the krug vorov which controls most crime in the Northern Hemisphere. Their agents have access to special drugs, both natural and synthetic, that allows them to push the human body beyond its limits for a limited amount of time. Thanks to their special training, they've also learned how to minimize secondary effects and avoid addiction.<br /> <br /> <b>Spartan Crisis Management:</b> The aberrant war left the world in chaos and, for the most part, made a mockery of conventional military forces. Army leaders all over the world watched in frustration as the aberrant massacred their soldiers as if they were nothing, and they could do little about it. The public and many politicians blamed them for not being able to protect their countries like they swore at their respective flags. It was quite the unfair attitude, since the truth is that without the valiant efforts of the military all over the world it could have been much worse. In any case, many brave soldiers found themselves on the streets, kicked out by the very same people they sacrificed their bodies and minds to defend. Suffice to say, few took it well, but few listened to their protests or cared when they ended in poverty.<br /> But someone cared. Someone who had lived a similar experience, someone who wanted to give those that still had a sense of honor and duty another chance. That someone was a survivor of the society of Leonidas. He wanted to rebuild the society and had plenty of recruits available, but he would modernize it, get rid of the traditions that had costed them so much. That\u2019s how Spartan Crisis Management was born, a private military company specialized in high risk targets, including aberrants, their most hated foe. Their agents combine ancient techniques from the society of Leonidas with the most modern military training, resulting in one man army Assassins capable to adapt to any hostile situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T13:29:35-07:00","id":1493482,"title":"","content":"This is pretty sweet! Me likey!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T17:07:17-07:00","id":1493652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1490573-all-eras-some-lore-questions?p=1493312#post1493312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THE SIGNAL: Survived, they took some heavy hits, but their decentralized nature played in their favor by making it impossible to target their leadership. In fact, I would go as far as to say that the signal is the only society who managed to stay active after the war and even leading the new shadow. The Shanghai Accords would change that, sadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would Shanghai Accords change mode of operation of <b>The Signal</b>? They are literally VERY decentralised. And even with Host being rogue AI - he is <u>rogue</u> AI. He do not need to stick to Accords - he is rogue, in the end \ud83d\ude09 - he even can work just the same as previous. Only it becomes harder for him. I envision that Host then create his own 'children' AIs , just to help him run things smoothie with Signal itself. And yes, they are then all the time on the run - like <i><a href=\"https://www.gateworld.net/wiki/Tok&#39;ra\" target=\"_blank\">Tok'ra</a></i> from <b>Stargate SG-1</b>. \ud83d\ude0e<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-24-2022, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}